{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew","id":782476,"title":"[Ex3] Sidereal Update Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-08T13:45:56-08:00","id":782476,"title":"[Ex3] Sidereal Update Homebrew","content":"With the document now representing the current state of this project I will update the link here periodically:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Version 1.1</a> <hr />So we already have threads that are bringing (or have already brought) updates for Lunars, Alchemicals and Dragon Kings. So I thought that Sidereals should get some love too. This is going to be where I post my update for Sidereals. If anyone else is already doing one I'd love to hear about it though and see where we have approached things differently.<br /> <br /> I have ideas written up for pretty much the entire Sidereal charmset, but I have only just started to write up the actual charm text in the last couple of days so I only have a few finished. I'll post the first of them tomorrow and update this thread with more as and when I finish them. But to kick things off here is character creation for an agent of Heaven's Bureau of Fate (ie a non-Ronin). <hr /><br /> <u><b>Character Creation</b></u><br /> <b>Step 1: Character Concept and Caste</b><br /> \u2022 Consult with other players and come up with an appealing, heroic concept.<br /> \u2022 Pick out the Caste that fits best, and note down its anima effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 2: Attributes</b><br /> \u2022 Mark down one dot in each Attribute.<br /> \u2022 Divide 8 dots among primary Attributes, 6 dots among secondary Attributes, and 4 dots among tertiary Attributes (see p. 121).<br /> <br /> <b>Step 3: Abilities</b><br /> \u2022 Select five Caste Abilities from the relevant list.<br /> \u2022 All Sidereals begin with Martial Arts (though not Brawl) as a Favored Ability.<br /> \u2022 Select four other Favored Abilities, which may not be the same as Caste Abilities.<br /> \u2022 All Sidereals start with the following abilities: Awareness 2, Brawl 1, Bureaucracy 2, Linguistics 1, Lore 3, Martial Arts 2, Occult 2, Socialize 1, Stealth 1 and at least one dot in Archery, Melee or Thrown.<ul><li>Chosen of Journeys must also have: Athletics 2, Resistance 2 and Survival 2.</li> <li>Chosen of Serenity must also have: Craft or Performance 2, Medicine 2 and Presence 2.</li> <li>Chosen of Battles must also have: Athletics 2, Dodge 2 and War 2.</li> <li>Chosen of Secrets must also have: Integrity 2, Investigation 2 and Larceny 2.</li> <li>Chosen of Endings must also have Dodge 2, Integrity 2, Martial Arts 3 and Stealth 2.</li> </ul><br /> \u2022 Divide 14 dots among all Abilities. None may be raised higher than 3 without spending Bonus Points, and each Favored Ability must have at least one dot.<br /> \u2022 Assign four specialities<br /> <br /> <b>Step 4: Colleges</b><br /> \u2022 Sidereals start with 1 dot in each of their Maiden's colleges. Additionally they gain +1 dot in any college where they have the related ability at 3+, or +2 dots if they have the ability rated at 5.<br /> \u2022 Spend up to 7 dots on colleges.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 5: Merits</b><br /> \u2022 All Sidereals start with the Language (Old Realm), Martial Arts and Mentor (3) merits.<br /> \u2022 Spend up to 10 dots on Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 6: Charms</b><br /> \u2022 Select 15 Charms, keeping in mind their requirements.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 7: Intimacies</b><br /> \u2022 Choose at least four Intimacies, including at least one Defining Intimacy, one Major Intimacy, one positive Intimacy, and one negative Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 8: Bonus Points</b><br /> \u2022 Spend 18 Bonus Points.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 9: Finishing Touches</b><br /> \u2022 Record Essence rating (1), Personal Essence pool ([Essence x 2] + 9), Peripheral Essence pool ([Essence x 6] + 25), Health Levels (-0, -1, -1, -2, -2, -4, Incapacitated), and Willpower (5). <hr /><u><b>Caste Abilities</b></u><br /> <b>Journeys:</b> Athletics, Bureaucracy, Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival &amp; Thrown.<br /> <b>Serenity:</b> Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Medicine, Performance, Presence &amp; Socialize<br /> <b>Battles:</b> Archery, Athletics, Lore, Melee, Presence, Resistance &amp; War<br /> <b>Secrets:</b> Integrity, Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth &amp; Thrown<br /> <b>Endings:</b> Awareness, Brawl, Bureaucracy, Integrity, Medicine, Occult &amp; Stealth <hr /><br /> So because this is not a particularly interesting first post here are some of my personal thoughts on how Sidereals work. These are also the themes I am trying to keep to in this update, where I can.<ul><li>Sidereals have smaller dice pools than other exalted and can manipulate the vagaries of fate. This to me indicates that they can't as easily exceed mortal limitations in the same way as other exalted. So while a Sidereal can consistently be at the pinnacle of mortal ability they don't go much beyond that. Example: A sidereal can perform a feat of strength requiring strength 5 with ease (relatively). However they find it impossible to go beyond human capability and say lift and throw a yeddim.</li> <li>My count of how many charms there are in the Sidereal 'set', including some names that have been brought back from 1st Ed, sits at around 170. With individual abilities having between 5 and 9 charms. Once I've updated existing charms I may go back and add a couple to the smaller trees, but that will be after the first pass at least.</li> <li>Finally Sidereal charms generally don't do dice tricks (recurring re-rolls or double x's). This leads to them having similar 'average' rolls as other exalted, though with much lower variance. This also means that there is a far lower likelihood of a Sidereal having an exceptional result such as a Solar might get.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":8793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","user":"Grifftofer","date":". 01-07-2016, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:11:11-08:00","id":782487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew#post782476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Select five Caste Abilities from the relevant list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm eagerly awaiting your list of Caste Ability choices for Sidereals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:19:05-08:00","id":782493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew#post782476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So because this is not a particularly interesting first post here are some of my personal thoughts on how Sidereals work. These are also the themes I am trying to keep to in this update, where I can.<ul><li>Sidereals have smaller dice pools than other exalted and can manipulate the vagaries of fate. This to me indicates that they can't as easily exceed mortal limitations in the same way as other exalted. So while a Sidereal can consistently be at the pinnacle of mortal ability they don't go much beyond that. Example: A sidereal can perform a feat of strength requiring strength 5 with ease (relatively). However they find it impossible to go beyond human capability and say lift and throw a yeddim.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually fine with this as a lot of Sidereal concepts seem to focus on passing as Mortal. Also, Sidereals are all about subtle use of power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew#post782476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Generally the Sidereal Charms trees will stop at Essence 3, with only some Essence 4 effects. This combined with the smaller charmset (less than 200 charms) will be to funnel Sidereals into SMA for higher Essence powers as it has been in the background.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I don' t like this. Lack of Charms to me is a fault with how Sidereals works. Sidereals desperately need more charms that aren't broken or they don't have to share with other player splats. At the very least, they need a &quot;Stash my Weapon in Elsewhere&quot; Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:19:07-08:00","id":782494,"title":"","content":"I'd give Sidereals 1 extra point because of the new Brawl tax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:21:23-08:00","id":782495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew#post782476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally the Sidereal Charms trees will stop at Essence 3, with only some Essence 4 effects. This combined with the smaller charmset (less than 200 charms) will be to funnel Sidereals into SMA for higher Essence powers as it has been in the background.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like this, it means a return of the &quot;everyone favors MA&quot; etc. Sidereals shouldn't be <i>forced</i> into MA as the source of all higher-essence power, it should just be a good option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:31:53-08:00","id":782502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782493#post782493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don' t like this. Lack of Charms to me is a fault with how Sidereals works. Sidereals desperately need more charms that aren't broken or they don't have to share with other player splats. At the very least, they need a &quot;Stash my Weapon in Elsewhere&quot; Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782495#post782495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like this, it means a return of the &quot;everyone favors MA&quot; etc. Sidereals shouldn't be <i>forced</i> into MA as the source of all higher-essence power, it should just be a good option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do somewhat agree with you both. The issue for the moment is that unless I write a whole load of new charms for Sidereals, after converting what we have, there is no way to feasibly do it. I will say that I do have plans to expand on the trees to bring them up to around 10 charms each, but that will be for somewhere down the road and probably require me to get the aid of the community. As much as I'd love to have the time and energy to make the Sidereal charmset even half as expansive as the solar one it's a little beyond the scope of this conversion for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:35:14-08:00","id":782504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782502#post782502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I do somewhat agree with you both. The issue for the moment is that unless I write a whole load of new charms for Sidereals, after converting what we have, there is no way to feasibly do it. I will say that I do have plans to expand on the trees to bring them up to around 10 charms each, but that will be for somewhere down the road and probably require me to get the aid of the community. As much as I'd love to have the time and energy to make the Sidereal charmset even half as expansive as the solar one it's a little beyond the scope of this conversion for now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's completely understandable. Just don't list &quot;Having very few amount of high essence charms&quot; as a design feature of your Ex3 Sidereal update. It makes me irrationally scared that the developers will get the idea to do the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:37:10-08:00","id":782505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782502#post782502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do somewhat agree with you both. The issue for the moment is that unless I write a whole load of new charms for Sidereals, after converting what we have, there is no way to feasibly do it. I will say that I do have plans to expand on the trees to bring them up to around 10 charms each, but that will be for somewhere down the road and probably require me to get the aid of the community. As much as I'd love to have the time and energy to make the Sidereal charmset even half as expansive as the solar one it's a little beyond the scope of this conversion for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can explicitly bless player-homebrew of higher essence charms (if they are reached before more charms come out, or whatever). This doesn't contradict the closed charmset so long as they are homebrewing charms that &quot;have always existed&quot; rather than, <i>in-character</i>, developing them from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:45:33-08:00","id":782514,"title":"","content":"Fair points. I'll remove the offending section. Plus add in the extra point for abilities (Grrrr Brawl messing things up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:45:34-08:00","id":782515,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Sidereal Charms, I had this idea of having Sidereals being able to temporary steal/switch intimacies from/between other people. Not sure if that power(s) would be in Socialize, Presence, or Larceny. <br /> <br /> Yes/No/OMG! So overpowered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:47:32-08:00","id":782516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782514#post782514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair points. I'll remove the offending section. Plus add in the extra point for abilities (Grrrr Brawl messing things up).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Fuck that Brawl Tax. I what I have read of Ex3 so far, but the Brawl Tax is the only thing that made me go &quot;Fuck, Why?! What's the fucking Point!?!&quot;<br /> <br /> Though, I have considered just giving all Sidereals MA as a Caste Ability for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:51:54-08:00","id":782520,"title":"","content":"I actually had a similar idea for a parallel update I'm trying of Sidereal Martial Arts. It would be an update of Impersonal Personal Denature Sting in Border of Kaleidoscopic Logic and be a gambit that scrambles all their intimacies around, though they may pay willpower to protect one or more intimacies.<br /> <br /> A Larceny charm that allows the Sidereal to steal one temporarily sounds like great fun though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:58:42-08:00","id":782522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782516#post782516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah. Fuck that Brawl Tax. I what I have read of Ex3 so far, but the Brawl Tax is the only thing that made me go &quot;Fuck, Why?! What's the fucking Point!?!&quot;<br /> <br /> Though, I have considered just giving all Sidereals MA as a Caste Ability for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still considering making it favoured for all Sidereals (though leaving brawl separate). Wasn't sure whether to do so or not though due to traditionally Sids having only the 4 favoured abilities.<br /> <br /> Well here is what I've come up with for expanded ability choices for Sidereals. Only 7 for each caste as I see Sids being more focused than Solars, by design. Plus I wasn't sure what other abilities fit, whilst leaving each ability in a maximum of 2 castes. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><b>Journeys:</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Athletics</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Bureaucracy</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Resistance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Ride</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Sail</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Survival</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Thrown</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><b>Serenity:</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Craft</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Dodge</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Linguistics</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Medicine</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Performance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Presence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Socialize</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><b>Batles:</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Archery</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Athletics</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Dodge</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Lore</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Melee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Presence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">War</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><b>Secrets:</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Integrity</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Investigation</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Larceny</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Lore</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Occult</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Stealth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Thrown</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><b>Endings:</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Awareness</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Brawl</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Bureaucracy</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Integrity</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Medicine</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Occult</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Stealth</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":8793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","user":"Grifftofer","date":". 12-09-2015, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T15:03:59-08:00","id":782523,"title":"","content":"They look great! Personally, I would give Journeys Bureaucracy (Traveling and Trading requires paperwork) and Battles Lore (all good generals know their history).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T16:13:12-08:00","id":782543,"title":"","content":"The Brawl Tax? You mean the one point of Brawl required to be a Martial Artist? I figured that was justified on the account of &quot;If you're going to learn a Martial Art, know how to throw a punch without breaking your own thumb&quot;, but then again I'm one of the guys who after some play said &quot;Wow, those people who think the 4-dot Merit for Martial Arts is overpriced don't know what they're talking about, JESUS&quot;, so take what I say with enough salt to stop a Hungry Ghost.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though I do have one question... When you say this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew#post782476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Step 5: Merits</b><br /> \u2022 Spend up to 10 dots on Merits. All Sidereals start with the Language (Old Realm), Martial Arts and Mentor (3) merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean ten dots on Merits and you gain like eight dots of Merits free (Mentor 3, MA 4, Language 1 = 8) or do you mean &quot;Take Ten dots of Merits... After buying these required Merits, so you actually only have two&quot;? I'm inclined to go with the former on my personal grounds of &quot;Dude don't be a dick to your player&quot; mindset, but-<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-08-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T16:52:37-08:00","id":782554,"title":"","content":"MA is essentially already favoured for all Sidereals, so you might as well make it official. Give them the Merit for free too.<br /> <br /> I don't think Brawl should be auto-favoured though.<br /> <br /> The one dot of Brawl required to be a martial artist is weird because learning a martial art that lets you attack unarmed already gives you the basic fist-fighting competence that you need. And learning one that doesn't makes you wonder what any of this has to do with Brawl at all.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really affect the balance of anything, because the game's not fine-tuned enough to make single ability dots important balance-wise. But it is rather strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T23:29:54-08:00","id":782648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782523#post782523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They look great! Personally, I would give Journeys Bureaucracy (Traveling and Trading requires paperwork) and Battles Lore (all good generals know their history).</div> </div> </div> </div>Those actually fit better than my thoughts on the matter. I'll swap out Resistance in Battles (Dodge gets used for movement and so fits slightly better) and Lore in Journeys (Navigating bureaucracies is more fitting than knowing about where you're going).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782543#post782543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean ten dots on Merits and you gain like eight dots of Merits free (Mentor 3, MA 4, Language 1 = 8) or do you mean &quot;Take Ten dots of Merits... After buying these required Merits, so you actually only have two&quot;? I'm inclined to go with the former on my personal grounds of &quot;Dude don't be a dick to your player&quot; mindset, but-</div> </div> </div> </div>The former was certainly my intention, but I see how it can be read as the other. I'll break that bit down into two separate bullet points to make it clearer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T00:59:36-08:00","id":782674,"title":"","content":"So here are the first two completed charm trees. These were some of the easiest ones to do due to a number of them being in the Core pdf. Before that though there is one new keyword to include, that is quite important for Sidereals. <hr /> <b>New Keyword: Prayer Strip</b><br /> A Charm with this Keyword has a physical manifestation that, if destroyed ends the charm. If the prayer strip is destroyed before the end of the Charm's duration then the Sidereal is refunded 1 Willpower. A prayer strip has a Defence of (Dexterity + Dodge + Essence/2, round up). It cannot be targeted with <b>withering</b> attacks, has Hardness 10 and 15 [-0] health levels. The prayer strip does not suffer onslaught penalties to its Defense and activated prayer strips are always visible to powers that detect magic at work, even when those powers cannot normally detect the charms of Exalted. <hr /> <u><b>Archery (The Quiver)</b></u><br /> <b>Generalized Ammunition Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m; <b>Mins:</b> Archery 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Fire any small object\u2014a handful or dust, a flame, a rat\u2014as an arrow. If the attack is awarded a stunt, add its level in bonus dice to the attack\u2019s damage, or as success on the Initiative roll of a gambit. May have other effects at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.<br /> <br /> <b>Any Direction Arrow</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 2i; <b>Mins:</b> Archery 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Dual<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Sight along the lines of fate to convert any dice from Aiming to successes. <b>Withering</b> attacks also add these successes to their damage roll. Heavy cover is reduced to light; light cover is negated entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Every Direction Arrow</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m; <b>Mins:</b> Archery 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Any Direction Arrow<br /> The attack becomes undodgeable.<br /> <br /> <b>Opportune Shot</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m, 2i, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Archery 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Clash, Perilous, Withering Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Make a reflexive clash with a <b>withering</b> attack against any attack made from short or medium (but not close) range. Crashing an enemy with Opportune Shot allows the Sidereal to reflexively Aim for another attack against them.<br /> <br /> <b>Five Seasons Approach</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Archery 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Every Direction Arrow, Opportune Shot<br /> Make a <b>decisive</b> attack, adding up to (Essence) extra successes on the attack roll as dice of raw damage. The target number of the damage roll is lowered by one. Lower the target number another point at Initiative 12+, and another against a crashed enemy.<br /> <br /> <b>Many Missiles Bow Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m, 1wp, 1lhl; <b>Mins:</b> Archery 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform, Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Five Seasons Approach<br /> Archery-based attacks may convert up to (Essence) dice into successes, before rolling. Additionally the Sidereal may reflexively apply transformations to the arrow as it falls. The Sidereal gains one transformation upon purchasing this Charm and may learn additional transformations for 1 experience point each.<br /> <br /> Each arrow transformed in this manner costs 1 mote to shoot. \u201cArrows\u201d from Generalized Ammunition Technique are not valid targets for the transformation effect, neither are arrows made from the Five Magical Materials. Commonly known transformations include:<br /> <br /> - <b>Glass:</b> Targets must make a (Perception + Awareness) check at difficulty 2. Failure makes the attack a surprise attack.<br /> - <b>Life:</b> By spending 4i, the Sidereal may heal the target for one level of bashing or lethal damage.<br /> - <b>Snow:</b> It begins to snow out to Medium range of where the arrow fell. The character must renew this effect with at least one arrow per minute to maintain this effect.<br /> - <b>Grain:</b> A small patch of ripe wheat, enough to feed one person for a day, sprouts where the arrow lands.<br /> - <b>Rain of Fire:</b> Creates a fire that extends to Close range of where the arrow landed. The fire is an environmental hazard with Damage/Interval 2L/round and difficulty (Archery). The hazard lasts for (Essence) rounds. The duration and damage of the hazard may be augmented by shooting more arrows into the area. Each arrow adds 2L to the damage of the hazard and (Essence) to the number of rounds remaining. The damage may not be raised above 6L/round.<br /> - <b>Boulder:</b> By spending 2i; the attack, if successful, may knock the opponent back one range band, or knock them prone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Some comments on Archery. A significant amount of the work here was done for me as the charms were written up in the backer pdf. I honestly didn't feel that any of these charms were specifically broad or powerful enough that they should be split down into multiple charms so I just ported them straight over.<br /> - Every Direction arrow was a bit of a judgement call, I considered setting it up to be a stackable damage enhancer or even a decisive extra attack action. In the end I went for this as it is a relatively simple fit and it evokes there being arrows coming from every angle to hit you. There is also some precedent in the Unobstructed Blow of Brawl, which was an unblockable attack.<br /> - Many Missiles was a bit interesting too as I wanted prayer strips to be powerful, but not make the Sidereal all powerful by just adding successes. Hopefully the converting dice strikes a bit of a middle ground, but it could easily be too much for a scene-long. My small defense of my decision is that with the excellency a Sidereal can drop the target number far enough then 80% of dice are successes anyway so this doesn't really boost that too much, merely twist the probabilities a little (I hope). <hr /><br /> <u><b>Athletics</b></u><br /> <b>Burn Life</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins:</b> Athletics 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The Sidereal may add Intimacy non-charm dice to a feat of strength roll. The feat of strength must uphold/protect/advance the Intimacy in some way.<br /> <br /> <b>Hungry Touch</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>; <b>Mins:</b> Athletics 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Burn Life<br /> When performing a feat of strength to destroy an object the Sidereal reduces the target number of the action to 5.<br /> <br /> <b>Forgotten Earth</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m; <b>Mins:</b> Athletics 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> When performing a jumping-based movement roll (e.g Rise From Prone action) convert 2 dice to successes before rolling. This charm may be used to enhance other abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Inexorable Advance</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m,2i; <b>Mins:</b> Athletics 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Forgotten Earth, Burn Life<br /> Negate all wound or mobility penalties on a rush roll, and complete the movement instantly on a success, instead of waiting for the target to move. If the Sidereal attacks a character on the same turn she rushes them with Inexorable Advance, they take -1 Defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Unswerving Juggernaut Principle</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m (+2m, 1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Athletics 2, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Choose an intimacy that can reasonably be said to be upheld/protected/advanced by performing this rush/disengage. Gain +(Intimacy) soak for the turn. If the sidereal attacks a character on the same turn she rushes them with Unswerving Juggernaut Principle then on a successful attack she may knock them back one range band or knock them prone.<br /> <br /> By spending an additional 2 motes and 1 Willpower the Sidereal may extend the duration to one journey, during which she does not need to eat or sleep so long as she continues to run towards her destination. If the Sidereal is forced to stop or significantly deviate from her course, or is crashed, then this charm ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Forward Thinking Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>- (+5m, 1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Athletics 3, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Unswerving Juggernaut Principle<br /> By spending a surcharge of +5 motes and 1 willpower when activating Unswerving Juggernaut Principle the sidereal gains an extra +(Essence) soak as well as (Essence) hardness. Additionally the Unswerving Juggernaut Principle's duration is extended to (Intimacy) turns.<br /> <br /> <b>Invisible Motion</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Athletics 4, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Inexorable Advance, Forward Thinking Technique<br /> Each turn, the Sidereal gains a pool of (Athletics) Momentum that may be used to enhance physical actions (explicitly including non-Athletics rolls). Momentum may be used to convert a dice into a success before rolling, or to increase Defense by 1. Momentum may be saved for use on Defense, but Momentum does not carry over from turn to turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> Some comments on Athletics.<br /> - Burn Life I wanted to be something that could stack with excellencies rather than be a replacement for them, which is why it gives non-charm dice. I also thought that the idea of a Sidereal giving up some of his own life in order to protect something cherished or advance towards his goal was quite cool, so I made it intimacy based. I think the wording needs tidying up and clarifying, but I'm not sure how best to do that.<br /> - Unswerving Juggernaut I wanted to keep fairly similar, but I thought it could have an in combat use as well. So I made it able to enhance a rush/disengage. It doesn't directly make you more likely to succeed, but I think that making yourself better protected whilst doing so is pretty worthy of the charm.<br /> - Forward Thinking I think would work just as well as an essence 3 upgrade within Unswerving Juggernaut itself. If I get around to expanding on this later on I may do that and make Forward Thinking something else, but for now it is pretty much just a straight conversion of previous editions.<br /> - For Invisible Motion I decided to stick with the converting dice to successes mechanic, which I think I may use for all prayer strips that work in a similar way, It should allow a Sidereal to boost their combat ability without making them unassailable. <hr /> Anyway that's it for now. Look forward to seeing what people have to say about these","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T01:24:08-08:00","id":782684,"title":"","content":"You know, I would've attempted Sidereals if not for 2 things.<br /> <br /> 1) They're most likely going to come out after Lunars<br /> 2) Astrology<br /> <br /> The second was the thing put my head into the sand for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T02:09:15-08:00","id":782695,"title":"","content":"Rather than saying that &quot;this caste has to have two dots in this, this, and this&quot; and stuff... I think it'd be far better to just say that every Sidereal must have at least two dots in three of their Caste abilities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:25:24-08:00","id":782819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782648#post782648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lore in Journeys (Navigating bureaucracies is more fitting than knowing about where you're going).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Don't you know where you are going?!?&quot;<br /> &quot;Nah! Half the fun is figuring it out when I get there.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:34:12-08:00","id":782822,"title":"","content":"I have a draft of a 3e Sidereal set. Here's one thing that bugged me a little bit, writing it: Colleges aren't fun.<br /> <br /> I mean, <i>Destinies</i> are great fun, don't get me wrong. But Colleges are one more stat that you have to buy, that's fairly expensive, that you only rarely get to roll, and that - at best - is basically duplicating the way you've <i>already done that</i> for your Ability ratings. You could say, &quot;Well, but it's a Solar/Sidereal XP outlet,&quot; but Sids are already going to be wanting to pump as much of that as possible into Martial Arts - and that leads to an awkward position where they just don't buy Colleges.<br /> <br /> I ultimately decided to just let people use Ability scores anywhere they'd normally roll Colleges; we're currently testing that with one of my players. Do you have a design goal for keeping them in your revision?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:35:37-08:00","id":782824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782822#post782822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ultimately decided to just let people use Ability scores anywhere they'd normally roll Colleges; we're currently testing that with one of my players. Do you have a design goal for keeping them in your revision?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I'd house-rule colleges. Greater Insight into an Ability allows you to preform greater acts of Astrology relating to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:00:23-08:00","id":782841,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on the matter was to base college ratings slightly off of Abilities. Which is why I had the starting ratings be based off of the abilities somewhat. I also intend for colleges to be significantly cheaper, probably along the lines of what Scaenicus suggested in his Astrology hack (3xp per dot. Fixed, not exponential). I'm not entirely certain whether or not I'm just keeping it as a legacy of the old system or whether it should stay though. The only thing I will say is that colleges can be interpreted quite broadly in astrology so there is some suggestion that the ability itself is not the entirety of the college.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T03:04:58-08:00","id":783332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782824#post782824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is how I'd house-rule colleges. Greater Insight into an Ability allows you to preform greater acts of Astrology relating to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another working houserule is :<br /> - you buy dots for the whole astrological house and get all 5 colleges at that rating, for the same price. They cost just like virtues (2E) so the total XP cost to max the 5 houses would be just a little more (+25%) than maxing all 4 virtues. Seams reasonable.<br /> - Dots above the 1st were useless because you had a ton of ways to improve your rolls, so the +4 dice difference from 1 to 5 dots is ridiculous compared to the XP cost (30xp). To balance that you may want to let the player unlock resplendent charms depending on their rating (1dot for the first charm, 3 for the second and 5 for the 3rd)<br /> - I also find appropriate to make the sidereal roll his highest rating every 3 month to reduce paradox instead of the flat 1 paradox. And/Or use that roll for the wrapped dragonfly ritual.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T01:41:18-08:00","id":784007,"title":"","content":"So here is the next instalment of charms. It's taking me a bit longer than I hoped to get through them, but I'm building up a bit of momentum so things are getting quicker now.<br /> <br /> <hr /> <u><b>Brawl</b></u><br /> <b>Unobstructed Blow</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins:</b> Brawl 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The attack becomes unblockable.<br /> <br /> <b>Tolerant Strife</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Brawl 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The attack's dice pool does not suffer from wound, onslaught, flurry, environmental, or being prone penalties.<br /> <br /> <b>Horrific Wreath</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m;<b> Mins:</b> Brawl 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only, Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Unobstructed Blow, Tolerant Strife<br /> The Sidereal's unarmed attacks deal Lethal damage. If used to strike at inhabitants of Malfeas or the Underworld then the damage becomes Aggravated.<br /> <br /> <b>Crimson Palm Counterstrike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins:</b> Brawl 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only, Counterattack<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> This creates a Brawl counterattack that occurs after the attack result, but before the damage has been rolled. This functions as a decisive attack, but compare the number of successes on the damage roll of the counterattack and the regular attack. The character with the greater total inflicts the difference between those two numbers as damage. The character with the lesser total inflicts no damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Orchestration of Conflict</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>;<b> Mins:</b> Brawl 5, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Horrific Wreath, Crimson Palm Counterstrike<br /> In combat the Sidereal may spend motes instead of initiative on combat actions/weapon tags at a 1:1 ratio.<br /> <br /> <b>Easily Accepted Proposition Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>12m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Brawl 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip, Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Orchestration of Conflict<br /> The charm allows the Sidereal to use the following gambit against the leader of her opponents in a confrontation.<br /> <b>Twist of Fate (Difficulty Varies):</b> The difficulty of this gambit should be determined by the ST based on the absurdity of the circumstances the Sidereal lays out as coming to pass. For example a beleaguered Sidereal may use this charm near to the end of a major battle to say that reinforcements arrive in time to save her and her command. Difficulty 1 might be assigned to a group of 50 beaten and battered soldiers having force marched to the rescue arriving. Whereas a fresh well rested Legion with a close ally as commander arriving could well be Difficulty 9. Or higher. If the gambit is successful then the target has two options. They can either accept this coincidence in which case the circumstances play out as the Sidereal scripted. Or the target chooses to reject the new fate, in which case they take (Gambit's Difficulty + Essence) dice of Aggravated damage that ignores hardness. Use of a charm to reduce/nullify this effect completely blocks the damage, but the circumstance comes into effect as the Sidereal scripted. This charm may only be used once per scene. Also note that invoking higher difficulty gambits with this charm can invite paradox or censure.<br /> <br /> <hr /><u><b>Bureaucracy</b></u> <b>Slick Essence Replenishment</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>;<b> Mins:</b> Bureaucracy 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Whenever the Sidereal successfully influences a large group with Bureaucracy she gains (Essence) motes. This bonus may only be received once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Icy Hand</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m;<b> Mins:</b> Bureaucracy 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> A (Charisma + Bureaucracy) Instill action that gives the target bureaucrat a major principle of &quot;Perform my duties diligently&quot;. This intimacy lasts for 3 days, at which point it degrades to a minor principle, after 2 further days it disappears entirely. The intimacy created does not need a supporting intimacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Terminal Sanction</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>8m,1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Bureaucracy 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Icy Hand<br /> This charm forces a spirit to manifest and materialize before the Sidereal. The spirit is compelled to not dematerialize for the scene. Roll (Charisma + Bureaucracy) against a difficulty of a spirit's (Essence), success means that if the spirit 'dies' during the scene the Sidereal can make one of four choices.<br /> - Destroy the spirit utterly.<br /> - Bind the spirit to service for one task or a year and a day.<br /> - Bind the spirit into a temporary artifact of rating (Essence/2, round up), which lasts for a year and a day.<br /> - Let the spirit reform normally, knowing what the Sidereal could have done.<br /> If used against a demon this charm gives the Sidereal (Essence) non-charm dice on the (Charisma + Bureaucracy) roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Underling Invisibility Practice</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>12m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Bureaucracy 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The Sidereal becomes invisible to everyone who thinks they are her superior (hierarchically, socially etc). Those affected consider themselves unobserved for the purposes of the Sidereal's Read Intentions actions. Additionally against those affected the Sidereal's social influences count as unexpected. The Sidereal rolls (Dexterity + Bureaucracy) against any Awareness rolls to detect her with the observer taking a -(Essence) penalty to their dice pool. If Join Battle is rolled then the Sidereal counts as being in Stealth until they take a violent action.<br /> <br /> <b>Paralyzed Mandarin Inflection</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Bureaucracy 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Terminal Sanction<br /> The Sidereal may choose an Intimacy held by the leader of an organisation. This charm causes the Intimacy to spread through the organisation through the next day, week, month, or longer depending on the size of the organisation in question. As it spreads through the ranks the Intimacy reduces in intensity resulting in those at the lowest levels of a large organisation only having a Minor Intimacy, even if the leader has that same Intimacy at Defining.<br /> <br /> <b>End Debate</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m, 1wp, 1hl;<b> Mins:</b> Bureaucracy 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Paralyzed Mandarin Inflection, Underling Invisibility Practice<br /> Roll (Charisma + Bureaucracy) against the Resolve of everyone in the scene, success drains the will to argue or debate ending the scene. Those affected may spend (Essence/2, round up) willpower to resist it's effects. This charm may only be attempted once per scene.<br /> <br /> <hr /> <u><b>Craft</b></u><br /> <b>Elemental Vision</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> There are 5 versions of this charm, one for each of the elements. Different crafts resonate with different elements, so each element requires a different craft ability to buy the apprpriate charm:<br /> <b>Air:</b> calligraphy, jewelery making, glassblowing<br /> <b>Earth:</b> masonry, stone cutting, creating earthworks<br /> <b>Fire:</b> blacksmithing, creating ceramics<br /> <b>Wood:</b> carpentry, weaving, flower arranging<br /> <b>Water:</b> cooking, brewing, leather working<br /> The charm gives a Minor Tie of Respect for the Sidereal in any elementals, dragon-bloods or god of the corresponding element.<br /> <br /> <b>Elegant Patterns of Fate</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Once per day roll (Intelligence + Craft[Fate]). Each successes on the roll gains the Sidereal 1sxp.<br /> <br /> <b>Excellent Implementation of Objectives</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The Sidereal completes Basic and Major projects within minutes to hours.<br /> <br /> <b>Destiny-Knitting Entanglement</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 4, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Elegant Patterns of Fate<br /> After handling an object for an hour the Sidereal may bind it top her fate. A Sidereal may have up to (Essence) items bound to her in such a way. Thereafter the Sidereal may 2 motes to get a general description of the item's current circumstances. Given knowledge of the situation she may spend 2 motes to describe a reasonable method by which the item can be brought closer to her. Multiple uses of this ability over time allow the Sidereal to bring an item all the way across creation and into her grasp. In combat spending 2 motes and an appropriate stunt allows the Sidereal to call a lost object to her hand. The Sidereal may release the destiny of any object that no longer interests her reflexively.<br /> <br /> <b>Mending Warped Designs</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Excellent Implementation of Objectives<br /> Roll (Dexterity + Craft[Fate]) each success heals on health level that the target lost to a creature or effect of Malfeas, the Underworld or the Wyld. This charm can also be used to counter the direct effects of the Wyld. 3 successes are required to 'cure' every merit point of a Wyld induced mutation. Fifty successes can cleanse a small region of Wyld influence. This charm does not permit extended rolls, but multiple Sidereals can apply it in the same turn, adding their successes together.<br /> <br /> <b>Predestined Delivery Shaping</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>7m;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Destiny-Knitting Entanglement<br /> Upon finishing an object that she has crafted herself the Sidereal may activate this charm. Doing so binds the object to the fate of a chosen person or place. As long as the essence remains committed to this charm the object is guided by fate to join with that of the person or place it is bound to. The progress is measured by an extended (Wits + Craft[Fate]) roll, with an interval of 1 month and a goal number based upon the distance the item must travel. The goal number ranges from 1 for across a town to 20 or more to cross Creation. A botch indicates that the item has been destroyed or otherwise cannot proceed any further. The character knows when the object has reached it's intended destination. This charm may be used as a transfer method for Astrological Destinies as an alternative to touching the intended target, carrying the destiny until the intended receives it.<br /> <br /> <b>World-Shaping Artistic Vision</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Elemental Vision (Any 2)<br /> Each purchase of this charm allows to create a circumstance, with the same breadth as a speciality, during which she reduces the target number of all rolls by 1. The character may purchase this charm up to (Essence) times. Each time the charm must apply to a different circumstance. Only one instance of this charm may apply to any dice roll, but regular specialities can be used as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Implicit Construction Methodology</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>20m, 1wp, 1hl;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Predestined Delivery Shaping, Mending Warped Designs<br /> The Sidereal suffers a -2 penalty to all rolls using her hands while the charm is active. Craft rolls do not suffer this dice penalty and additionally the Sidereal does not suffer penalties for lack of tools or workspace. All dice in the pool of a Craft roll come up as successes. Moonsilver reacts dangerously with this charm and must thus be worked normally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T04:38:56-08:00","id":784056,"title":"","content":"This is g\u0336l\u0336o\u0336r\u0336i\u0336o\u0336u\u0336s\u0336 fateful!<br /> <br /> I just have small things to say :<br /> - <b>horrific wreath </b>: why not have wyld in the list too?<br /> - <b>Easily accepted proposition stance </b>: I don't know if dealing direct damage would be OK. As you can see, you have to handle exceptions like the enemy trying to mitigate the damage. Maybe replace it by init gain/loss/transfert. Of course numbers would need tweaking to balance power loss. (also for the rest of the scene you would deal aggravated damage with all your attacks against the leader in that case). But the Idea is great just like the whole tree.<br /> - <b>Slick Essence Replenishment : </b>Maybe raise it to essence+magnitude, because my first impression is it's a little weak and doesn't reward targeting larger social groups. Players will be inclined to &quot;spam&quot; it on the smallest groups applicable<br /> - <b>End debate </b>: Works in combat? Good way to screw people that commited a lot of resources in scenelong effects (sid bastards ^^).<br /> - <b>Destiny-Knitting Entanglement :</b> Maybe too vague in defining how progress is made.<br /> - <b>Mending Warped Designs </b>and <b>Predestined Delivery Shaping</b> : I'm missing some 2.5E tweaks. The original versions feel like they're not useful enough for the XP investment.<br /> - <b>Implicit Construction Methodology</b> : I never understood the reson for the moonsilver clause :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:40:31-08:00","id":784081,"title":"","content":"I just have small things to say :<br /> - <b>horrific wreath </b>: why not have wyld in the list too?<br /> <i><span style=\"color:#B22222\">No specific reason. I just used the particulars from the 1ed version of the charm, which only specified inhabitants of Malfeas/the Underworld. I don't particularly see any reason the charm couldn't also affect those of the Wyld too though.</span></i><br /> <br /> - <b>Easily accepted proposition stance </b>: I don't know if dealing direct damage would be OK. As you can see, you have to handle exceptions like the enemy trying to mitigate the damage. Maybe replace it by init gain/loss/transfert. Of course numbers would need tweaking to balance power loss. (also for the rest of the scene you would deal aggravated damage with all your attacks against the leader in that case). But the Idea is great just like the whole tree.<br /> <i><span style=\"color:#B22222\">That is a fair point. Maybe something like (Gambit's Difficulty + Essence) withering damage dice, which ignores soak. Plus some lesser effect on the leader's subordinates? Lower of (Brawl) or (Gambit's Difficulty + Essence/2) maybe?</span></i><br /> <br /> - <b>Slick Essence Replenishment : </b>Maybe raise it to essence+magnitude, because my first impression is it's a little weak and doesn't reward targeting larger social groups. Players will be inclined to &quot;spam&quot; it on the smallest groups applicable<br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>I'd certainly consider doing something like that, as the other Essence Replenishment charms are mostly the same. However I've not seen anything that gives organisations a Magnitude, I may have missed it though. But based on that I've made most of my effects on social groups relatively free-form. If there is a page reference that someone can point me to that says otherwise I'll adjust things, but that was my impression at least.</i></span><br /> <br /> - <b>End debate </b>: Works in combat? Good way to screw people that commited a lot of resources in scenelong effects (sid bastards ^^).<br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>I hadn't specifically thought of (or entirely intended) that usage. Though it does sound like a very Sidereal thing to do :P</i></span><br /> <br /> - <b>Destiny-Knitting Entanglement :</b> Maybe too vague in defining how progress is made.<br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>Yeah I could probably define it better. I'm not too certain how exactly though, unless I just take the mechanics from Predestined Delivery Shaping.</i></span><br /> <br /> - <b>Mending Warped Designs </b>and <b>Predestined Delivery Shaping</b> : I'm missing some 2.5E tweaks. The original versions feel like they're not useful enough for the XP investment.<br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>You could well be right. I hadn't had a chance to check through the scrolls of Errata recently. I probably should have :S Maybe I can find some way of enhancing them somewhat. The thing is that both can be quite powerful narratively so I don't want to take them too far.</i></span><br /> <br /> - <b>Implicit Construction Methodology</b> : I never understood the reson for the moonsilver clause :/<br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>I think it was partly to limit Sidereals in what they can make. It would mean that they cannot easily make artifacts with certain themes. I also wanted to keep it as a minor restriction, because the charm is quite powerful generally. Not too much I think though.</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:20:42-08:00","id":784179,"title":"","content":"Ok. Here are a couple more abilities to tide you over the weekend, as I likely won't have a chance to do too much work on this. I'll try to drop in occasionally to reply if anyone has anything to say though, and there is always the slim possibility of me getting some stuff done on the train and in spare moments.<br /> <br /> <hr /> <b><u>Dodge</u></b><br /> <b>Absence</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Dodge 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Negate all wound or mobility penalties on a disengage roll, and complete the movement instantly on a success, instead of waiting for the target to move.<br /> <br /> <b>Duck Fate</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m;<b> Mins:</b> Dodge 4, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Absence<br /> Once per scene the Sidereal may dodge any attack without contest. This may even be used to evade uncountable recurring damage or environmental hazards. This charm may be reset by dodging 3 decisive attacks from dangerous opponents.<br /> <br /> <b>Avoidance Kata</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m;<b> Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Roll (Dexterity + Dodge) dice against a difficulty of (3 + turns already taken in the scene). Success causes the Sidereal to vanish, reappearing somewhere else she might have plausibly gone today instead. Witnesses remember the Sidereal being present, but also remember that she was never present at all, and find this contradiction unremarkable. Once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Trouble Reduction Strategy</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Dodge 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Avoidance Kata<br /> Reflexively protect all allies in close range with Evasion, as with a Defend Other action. Allows them to be included in withdrawal via Avoidance Kata, but each individual carried along raises the difficulty by 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 15m, 1wp, 1hl;<b> Mins:</b> Dodge 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Duck Fate, Trouble Reduction Strategy<br /> The Sidereal may move all habitations and general terrain within (Essence) miles with her as she moves. Every hour of travel inflicts 2 levels of bashing damage. Creation fills in the gap left behind with reasonable scenery for that region. Additionally 'important' terrain cannot be overwritten so a Manse, Demesne or similar will be incorporated into the new landscape.<br /> <br /> <hr /> <u><b>Integrity</b></u><br /> <b>Unwavering Well-Being Meditation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Integrity 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Subtract the Sidereal\u2019s current temporary Willpower from the raw damage of a <b>decisive </b>attack roll against him. The target number of the damage roll is raised by one.<br /> <br /> <b>Preservation of Resolve</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -(+2m);<b> Mins:</b> Integrity 2, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> This charm allows the Sidereal to activate her Integrity Excellency to enhance another's Resolve, by paying a 2 mote surcharge. The beneficiary of this charm must be touched in order to activate it.<br /> <br /> <b>Creation Preserving Will</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Integrity 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Unwavering Well-Being Meditation<br /> Increase the target number of a social influence targeting the Sidereal by 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Unhearing Dedication</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Integrity 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Creation Preserving Will, Preservation of Resolve<br /> Select one intimacy that relates to an officially sanctioned plan. This intimacy may be used in a Decision Point, even if it was used to increase the character's resolve against the same social influence. The Intimacy supported by this charm may be reflexively changed to another that fulfils the requirements, should the plan be finished, or the Sidereal may spend one experience to change it even if the plan hasn't been finished.<br /> <br /> <b>Death of Self Meditation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m;<b> Mins:</b> Integrity 4, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One day<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Unhearing Dedication<br /> As a final defense against a social influence instead of spending willpower. The player then chooses a single Defining Intimacy, which the Storyteller then builds a personality around. The character is then forced to become this new personality for one day and the social influence is resisted. New personalities created by this charm may be eccentric or extreme in order to better resist certain social influences.<br /> <br /> <b>One Direction Invocation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 15m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Integrity 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Death of Self Meditation<br /> When activating this charm the Sidereal names a task that this charm is intended to assist with and pays her name as collateral to see the task completed. For the charm's duration she becomes even more difficult to remember with people suffering an additional -3 dice penalty to rolls to remember her, on top of Arcane Fate. The character gains (Integrity) [-0] health levels and multiplies her healing rate by (Essence). However all dice pools to accomplish actions that aren't directly related to completing the named task are reduced by 3 dice. If the prayer strip is destroyed then the character loses the benefit of the charm but does not regain her name until she finishes the named task. If the task ever becomes impossible then the character's name is lost forever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:27:38-08:00","id":784187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=784179#post784179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Avoidance Kata</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m;<b> Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Roll (Dexterity + Dodge) dice against a difficulty of (3 + turns already taken in the scene). Success causes the Sidereal to vanish, reappearing somewhere else she might have plausibly gone today instead. Witnesses remember the Sidereal being present, but also remember that she was never present at all, and find this contradiction unremarkable. Once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the original roll had a willpower cost to remember? So, if you payed the willpower, you'd remember the Sidereal. Maybe it was an integrity roll. If you didn't, the Sidereal was never there. Of course, there was a limit of two actions before you couldn't activate the charm. I like the increased difficulty for the longer you stay in the scene. <br /> <br /> I miss the Regain Motes Integrity charm. Yet I can't think of a way to convert it over since it was very much tied to Virtues. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:49:37-08:00","id":784199,"title":"","content":"I won't pretend to have come up with that, or Trouble Reduction Strategy as both were in the leaked copy of the core book. Those charms/characters that were cut for space have provided additional points in order to extrapolate other Sidereal charms.<br /> <br /> As for the essence regain charms. In 1st edition they were spread over a number of abilities (Bureaucracy, Presence, Performance and Socialize), which is the approach I've taken with this conversion. Slick Essence Replenishment is already above as an example of the others, which would work in much the same way but for the other abilities listed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T05:54:39-08:00","id":787301,"title":"","content":"Ok. So I'm back with a small update today. I'm trying to give full abilities where I can, but I've been jumping around in the writing too much over the last few days to really be able to do that. <hr /> <u><b>Investigation</b></u><br /> <b>Marvellous Inclusion of Details</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Investigation 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Auspicious Prospects for (Caste)<br /> The Sidereal gets +1 non-charm success; maximum (Essence); for every previous case/profile action that the Sidereal has made in trying to solve one case/mystery.<br /> <br /> <b>Efficient Secretary Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m;<b> Mins:</b> Investigation 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Call up an emerald spider that retrieves any objective fact or piece of information that is publicly available and known.<br /> <br /> <b>Research Assistant Invocation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Investigation 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Efficient Secretary Technique<br /> The Sidereal turns a nearby plant into an assistant, who is focused on investigation and research. The new assistant has the stats of a two-dot Retainer and speaks the same language as the Sidereal. The transformation lasts for 5 days, before the assistant turns back into a plant.<br /> <br /> <b>Embracing Life Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Investigation 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Five days<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Marvellous Inclusion of Details, Research Assistant Invocation<br /> The sidereal buries the prayer strip and rolls (Charisma + Investigation). The successes rolled are the number of pieces of information the Sidereal gets about solving a quandary posed when the prayer strip is buried. The Sidereal may end the charm early, for every day less than the duration the roll loses 1 success.<br /> <hr />As you can see this set is missing Auspicious Prospects for (Caste) that is due to me struggling with whether to just bring it straight over with no changes or not. I was considering making it more like Watchman's Infallible Eye for the five astrological houses, but thought that would be too broad for a single charm. Would appreciate some suggestions if anyone has any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T06:37:15-08:00","id":787321,"title":"","content":"I'm not blaming you but I still find it frustrating that for a splat that it universally known for spying and meddling with secrets (even when they're not from the secrets caste) sids get such a small and weak investigation charm tree.<br /> <br /> As for Auspicious Prospects for (Caste), IIRC those charms didn't really leave any room for clever use. You just spend the motes and pray your ST gives you something decent to work with. Really the kind of charm I dislike the most (AND i find it not fiting for the sidereal &quot;style&quot;).<br /> It also sound so much like a justification for the ST to give arbitrary information for sidereal NPC = not a charm suited for PCs.<br /> <br /> Edit : <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a> thank you for reminding me this too. I would +99 you if I could.<br /> Investigation should at least have a decypher charm as it totally fits both the ability AND the maiden. Cypher charms technically belong more to linguistics but it could be placed in investigation instead as usual for sid charm trees.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":2172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","user":"Jack In The Box","date":". 12-16-2015, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T06:58:57-08:00","id":787330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=787321#post787321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not blaming you but I still find it frustrating that for a splat that it universally known for spying and meddling with secrets (even when they're not from the secrets caste) sids get such a small and weak investigation charm tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, having two agents spying on different sides is totally in Sidereal's wheelhouse, but there is no way to communicate with them. I always thought it was a crime that Sidereals didn't have any cool cipher charms (I think Avoiding the Truth Technique is the closest if used creatively). There was a scene where my Sidereal had to communicate something to another Sidereal in a new Resplendent Destiny. I had to figure out a way to talk to this &quot;stranger&quot; without giving away information that my Solar companion would seem odd to tell this random dude. (I ended up singing a song that gave the NPC the gist of the situation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-16-2015, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:15:44-08:00","id":787346,"title":"","content":"Well I am always happy to take on suggestions for expanding the charm tree later on. I certainly don't see any problems with the Sidereal charmset getting bigger in general, especially with the Solar charms numbering around 700+. Having said that however, any ideas for making Auspiscious Prospects better/more in theme?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:24:45-08:00","id":787348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=787346#post787346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I am always happy to take on suggestions for expanding the charm tree later on. I certainly don't see any problems with the Sidereal charmset getting bigger in general, especially with the Solar charms numbering around 700+. Having said that however, any ideas for making Auspiscious Prospects better/more in theme?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm just venting about the cipher thing to be honest. I don't expect you to make charms up for all of my crazy ideas! lol<br /> <br /> Auspiscious Prospects reads to me as 'Find Plot' charm. I'd be tempted make it a permanent charm that is attuned to a Sidereal's Patron, so the ST can feed your character plot though the charm. Sort of a &quot;My Spiders Senses are Tingling. This individual needs to travel!&quot; That may be more of an Awareness Charm though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:30:03-08:00","id":787351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=787321#post787321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit : <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a> thank you for reminding me this too. I would +99 you if I could.<br /> Investigation should at least have a decypher charm as it totally fits both the ability AND the maiden. Cypher charms technically belong more to linguistics but it could be placed in investigation instead as usual for sid charm trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more Lore for the Cypher charm. You can change fate to send a message though an old book/letter/newspaper/etc. The text has been there forever, so obviously it has nothing to do with last week's events. It's just a coincidence! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-16-2015, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:39:11-08:00","id":787361,"title":"","content":"Your idea of the cypher charm actually made me reconsider the relatively boring idea I had for Avoiding the Truth Technique (which is moving back to Lore where it was in 1st Ed). It's looking more like a combo of Letter Within a Letter and Subtle Speech Method, but fallible and not requiring you to know the target now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T13:28:31-08:00","id":787604,"title":"","content":"<b>Pho Cart Methodology*</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Motes, 1 WP;<b> Mins:</b> Bureaucracy 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Seven Days<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The Sidereal can set up a small established business in a town. This Business will neither make or lose money. Residents will patron the business as if it was always there. At the end of the charm's duration, the business will vanish and the town's inhabitants will not remember its existence.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence 4+</b>: The duration of the business is extended to the end of the current story line. <br /> <br /> <b>Repetitive History Assurance</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Motes;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>????<br /> <b>Duration:</b> ???<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>???<br /> Everyone knows history is doomed to repeat itself and clever Sidereals take advantage of this assumption. The Sidereal can alter the fate of a book or document to send a message about current events to another individual. Anyone besides the intended recipient assumes the altered passage has nothing to do with current events.<br /> <br /> <b>Discordant String's Echo</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Investigation 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> ????<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>????<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Marvelous Inclusion of Details<br /> The Sidereal can tune into the threads of Fate of a room and relive events that happened in that room within the past week. The Sidereal is unaware of their present surroundings while using this charm.<br /> <br /> *I'm tempted to rename the charm Cabbage Cart Methodology after everyone's favorite <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BiMhue3iSd4\" target=\"_blank\">Cabbage Cart Merchant</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-16-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T15:54:29-08:00","id":787677,"title":"","content":"I do like the looks of those and may well steal them later on. The only thing I would say is in relation to Discordant String's Echo. Might it need some kind of limit to it to stop it being 'I solve any mystery that is less than a week old in one charm'? Possibly something along the lines of: &quot;The images shown are based on the pattern spiders' collective memory of events. People are not important as individuals to the pattern spiders, but merely as fates to be progressed as such all features are hazy and indistinct enough to be unrecognisable.&quot; That way you'd be able to use the charm to discover what happened, how where and when but not who or why. To me that would at least mean you need to do some investigative work rather than just arriving at an answer because you used the charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T16:01:37-08:00","id":787687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=787677#post787677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the looks of those and may well steal them later on. The only thing I would say is in relation to Discordant String's Echo. Might it need some kind of limit to it to stop it being 'I solve any mystery that is less than a week old in one charm'? Possibly something along the lines of: &quot;The images shown are based on the pattern spiders' collective memory of events. People are not important as individuals to the pattern spiders, but merely as fates to be progressed as such all features are hazy and indistinct enough to be unrecognisable.&quot; That way you'd be able to use the charm to discover what happened, how where and when but not who or why. To me that would at least mean you need to do some investigative work rather than just arriving at an answer because you used the charm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very True, though sometimes the mystery isn't &quot;whodunit&quot; but &quot;why was it done?&quot; Another option would be to limited the charm to one person's recollection of the events instead of the room?<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I like the idea that pattern spiders don't see people as individuals but as patterns. A sidereal may get &quot;The Man who always buys pastries at 7am on Tuesdays&quot; as a clue, instead of his name.<br /> <br /> I'll admit to not being sure about the costs or ability/essence level of the charms. I'm not yet a good judge of how powerful a charm is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T16:58:28-08:00","id":787715,"title":"","content":"Glad you like the idea. I have to say it felt right as I wrote it.<br /> <br /> I think the costs and requirements for charms are somewhat flexible. Less so for combat charms due to the nature of combat, but other areas generally have less mechanical precision and greater ST input so the exact cost isn't as important.<br /> <br /> Anyway here are a few more bits to look at. As always comments and advice are always welcome. <hr /> <u><b>Larceny</b></u><br /> <b>Thought Swiping Distraction</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Larceny 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Reduce the target's Guile by (Larceny/2, round up) when making a Read Intentions action.<br /> <br /> <b>Masque of the Uncanny</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m;<b> Mins:</b> Larceny 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Thought Swiping Distraction<br /> The Sidereal may disguise herself as a fae, ghost or demon without suffering the normal penalties on the disguise roll. The disguise is impervious to mundane senses for (Essence) scenes, but can be pierced by inhuman senses with a roll as normal. Senses heightened to supernatural levels by Charms such as Keen Sight Discipline have a chance to pierce this deception as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Honourable Thief Spirit</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Larceny 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Criminals who interact with her count as having a minor intimacy of trust or admiration (the players choice) towards the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereal Shell Games</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Larceny 5, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Honourable Thief Spirit<br /> Roll (Wits + Larceny) against the target's (Essence) for each threshold success the Sidereal may steal from the target's soak or one of their ability dice pools, up to (Essence) soak/dice. The Sidereal may only steal from dice pools in which they have points in the related college. The target may spend one willpower to reduce the maximum available to steal to (Essence/2, round up). The target's soak/dice pool is reduced by the amount stolen and the Sidereal increases their same trait by the same amount. The decrease of a dice pool does not alter the number of dice that the target may add through charms or other magic. This charm may be used once per scene, unless reset by crashing the target of this charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Name Pilfering Practices</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Larceny 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinites<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Masque of the Uncanny<br /> The charm allows the Sidereal to use the following gambit, using an attack pool of (Dexterity + Larceny).<br /> <b>Thief of Memory (Difficulty 6):</b> If successful this gambit steals the target's name so that only the Sidereal may think, write or speak it. This means that when the victim leaves someone's presence they must roll (Wits + Integrity) to remember who the victim is, this roll suffers a -3 dice penalty, but is only difficulty one. The effects of the victim's actions remain, but people don't necessarily attribute those actions to the victim. This makes it difficulty for the victim to build long term relationships as memories of who they are fade quickly.<br /> This charm may be used outside of combat by touching the victim and succeeding at a (Manipulation + Larceny) roll against a difficulty of the target's Essence. Essence is only committed to this charm if the gambit is successful.<br /> <br /> <b>Dream Confiscation Approach</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m, 1wp (+4m);<b> Mins:</b> Larceny 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Name Pilfering Practice<br /> The charm allows the Sidereal to use the following gambit, using an attack pool of (Dexterity + Larceny).<br /> <b>Touch of the Dreamless (Difficulty 5):</b> If successful this gambit steals the target's ability to gain restful sleep. This means that the victim can no longer recover willpower from sleeping. Trivial opponents suffer from this affliction for the rest of their lives. Non-trivial opponents recover after (Essence) months. If the victim has higher Essence than the Sidereal then this period drops to (Essence) weeks. Using this charm against one of the fair folk causes (Essence) aggravated damage that ignores hardness in addition to the other effects.<br /> This charm may be used outside of combat at a surcharge of 4 motes at which point it only requires that the Sidereal touch the victim and succeed a (Wits + Larceny) roll against a difficulty of the target's Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Conning Chaos Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Larceny 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Varies<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sidereal Shell Games, Dream Confiscation Approach<br /> Roll (Manipulation + Larceny) against difficulty target's Essence, the victim is cursed for a number of months equal to the roll's threshold successes. The curse causes Fair Folk or Wyld creatures to seek him out, possibly bestowing 'favours' on the victim.<br /> The victim gets to make an extended (Intelligence + Lore) roll with an interval of one month. If the victim accrues 6 successes they realise that the prayer strip they saw when being cursed is the cause of the curse. Upon reaching 12 successes the victim is able to figure out the exact location of the prayer strip.<br /> For each month that the victim remains cursed one square mile of the Boardermarches is ceded to Creation. This region is now a true part of creation and suffers no long-term maladies from having been a part of the Wyld. <hr /> <u><b>Linguistics</b></u><br /> <b>Favourable Inflection Procedure</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Linguistics 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Sidereal perfectly mirrors the cadence and inflection of an area giving locals a temporary minor intimacy of friendly familiarity towards her. This does not allow the Sidereal to communicate with people in a language she does not know, merely make people she can communicate with more accepting of her.<br /> <br /> <b>Blue Vervain Binding</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1xp;<b> Mins:</b> Linguistics 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Favourable Inflection Procedure<br /> The Sidereal recites a minute-long blessing in the Old Tongue. Roll (Intelligence + Linguistics) against a difficulty of 5. Success binds the fates of two beings so that they can understand each other forever after regardless of their respective languages. The extent of the communications is limited only by intelligence of the two creatures. Trying to teach a Tyrant Lizard the finer points of pacifism may be an exercise in futility.<br /> <br /> <b>Hot Eyed Snake Whispering</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Linguistics 4, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Written Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The intended recipient of the missive will always be able read and understand this letter. Regardless of if they have 0 dots in Linguistics or no languages in common with the Sidereal. Others attempting to read the text must roll (Intelligence + Linguistics) against a difficulty of the Sidereal's (Essence) in order to interpret it successfully.<br /> <br /> <b>Abandoned Words Curse</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m;<b> Mins:</b> Linguistics 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Hot Eyed Snake Whispering<br /> Roll (Wits + Linguistics) against the target's (Resolve). Success removes one language from the target, chosen by the Sidereal. The target no longer reads, writes, speaks or understands the chosen language. The victim may re-learn the language with time and effort (usually a minimum of one month to re-learn a native tongue).<br /> <br /> <b>Ice and Fire Binding</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m;<b> Mins:</b> Linguistics 5, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Blue Vervain Binding, Abandoned Words Curse<br /> At the end of a ceremony that takes one hour roll (Intelligence + Linguistics) against a difficulty of 4 + intended spirit's (Essence). Success creates a spirit or elemental of fire with a defining intimacy to spread joy, health and pleasure. This intimacy is protected from being weakened for one season plus one month per threshold success on the original roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Lover's Oath</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 20m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Linguistics 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Ice and Fire Binding<br /> The two, willing, beneficiaries of this charm roll (Intelligence + Linguistics). If between them they achieve 5 successes then the Lover's Oath comes into effect. The prayer strip turns into a pair of starmetal rings set with a sapphire, which the wearers cannot attempt to remove. Once the rings are in place then each may spend each other's Willpower and Essence as if it where their own. Essence spent counts as Peripheral for the purposes of anima flare. Once per day either may accept the wounds of the other transferring up to (Essence) damaged health levels to themselves from their partner. Health levels transferred are taken from the Incapacitated, then -4 levels, then -2 levels etc. Aggravated damage may not be transferred. <hr /> <u><b>Lore</b></u><br /> <b>Systematic Understanding of Everything</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive/Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Any dice provided by a speciality are converted into successes before the roll is made. This charm may be used with other abilities. If used to enhance a defence then the charm doesn't add to the Sidereal's defense, but causes an attack with 0 threshold successes to miss.<br /> <br /> <b>The Methodology of Secrets</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive/Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Systematic Understanding of Everything<br /> The Sidereal may choose three specialities to apply to any of her abilities for the duration of the charm. These work as normal specialities and thus may not stack with regular specialities.<br /> <br /> <b>Of Truths Best Unspoken</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Spend three hours in meditation to make a recall knowledge roll about any topic to learn what its importance will be in the future, from the perspective of the end of the Second Age. Once per story.<br /> <br /> <b>Avoiding the Truth Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Of Truths Best Unspoken<br /> The Sidereal may communicate a second message as subtext during another conversation/missive. The secret message may not have content longer than the spoken/written message. Attempts to uncover the secret message are made as an opposed (Intelligence + Lore) roll with the opponent suffering -(Essence) dice.<br /> <br /> <b>Of Things Desired and Feared</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> After spending one month advising or teaching someone the Sidereal may activate this charm to give the beneficiary of their advice/teaching a minor intimacy of fear or desire towards something of the Sidereal's choice. The ST should be fairly liberal in interpreting the intimacy, for example an intimacy of &quot;Bring down the Realm&quot; could be seen as a desire to end the Realm's corrupting influence on the Threshold.<br /> <br /> <b>Of the Shape of the World</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Of Things Desired and Feared<br /> After spending one hour in meditation the Sidereal may read about a place, person or object's future. Roll (Intelligence + Lore) threshold successes give the Sidereal one piece of information about the target's future. The difficulty of the roll is based on the area that the Sidereal studies. At difficulty 1 the Sidereal discerns information from the whole of the target's life. Difficulty 3 narrows the length of time down to a specific year. Difficulty 5 narrows it down to a specific month. This charm may only be used once per story for a given target.<br /> <br /> <b>Of Horrors Best Unknown</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m (+1wp);<b> Mins:</b> Lore 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Of the Shape of the World<br /> Roll (Dexterity + Lore) against a difficulty of the target's (Essence). Success inflicts a curse on the target that makes it more likely that people will succeed against them. The curse reduces the target number of any rolls against the victim by one for one scene. The scene must happen within one year and a day of the curse being placed or it fades away. By spending a surcharge of 1 willpower when using this charm the Sidereal may extend the time period in which the scene can occur to indefinite.<br /> <br /> <b>Of Secrets Yet Untold</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Avoiding the Truth Technique<br /> Reduce the strength of intimacy required to Persuade a spirit to perform a task/action by one level. This charm may only be used once per story on a given target.<br /> <br /> <b>Transcendent Hatchet of Fate</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 16m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Lore 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> The Methodology of Secrets, Of Horrors Best Unknown, Of Secrets Yet Untold<br /> Roll (Intelligence + Lore) against a difficulty of the target's (Guile + Essence). Success writes the target's worst fear into a prayer strip. Thereafter the Sidereal may read out the contents of the prayer strip to the target. The target understands the Sidereal's words regardless of the language being spoken and loses (Essence/2, round down) Willpower. The fate read out by the Sidereal is now fated to happen and cannot be averted by the victim's actions. The ST should come up with an alternative if the suggested destiny is not possible. Essence committed to this charm is only committed until the Sidereal reads out the contents of the prayer strip. If the Sidereal releases the commitment before reading out it's contents the prayer strip fades into nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":8793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","user":"Grifftofer","date":".  Being an idiot and spelling Lore, 'Linguistics'. 12-17-2015, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:04:20-08:00","id":787769,"title":"","content":"A huge thank you from me to you. The homebrew you and others are putting up is going to make it possible to run the sort of games I want to run without waiting years. That said, any chance (when you finish) of throwing this into a document on google drive or other filesharing platform? The forums are difficult to search on my phone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:40:24-08:00","id":787787,"title":"","content":"I really like what you're doing here, this is really useful.<br /> I am slightly uncertain about completely changing Avoiding the Truth Technique's use from anti-persuasion to secret messaging, but I think it could be made to work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T23:51:15-08:00","id":787882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=787769#post787769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A huge thank you from me to you. The homebrew you and others are putting up is going to make it possible to run the sort of games I want to run without waiting years. That said, any chance (when you finish) of throwing this into a document on google drive or other filesharing platform? The forums are difficult to search on my phone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I'm moving the charms into a document as I work through them so I'll compile that with the character creation stuff and other bits when I finish and put that somewhere accessible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=787787#post787787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like what you're doing here, this is really useful.<br /> I am slightly uncertain about completely changing Avoiding the Truth Technique's use from anti-persuasion to secret messaging, but I think it could be made to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fair concern as it is pretty much one of the iconic Sidereal charms. The only problem is that I had difficulty making it not boring in terms of what it does. Plus the fact that you can mostly stunt the telling the truth in such a way as to convince a person you're lying. So when wonderandawe suggested a cypher charm it felt like a good match, if a bit of a change in theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T02:17:42-08:00","id":787932,"title":"","content":"Here's the next two abilities. May be a day or two before I get the next few sorted as they (Occult, Performance and Presence) are mostly incomplete at this point. <hr /><u><b>Medicine</b></u> <b>Smooth Transition</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m;<b> Mins:</b> Medicine 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> A living creature, who is willing to die, can be killed instantly and painlessly. The creature's body may not be raised as a zombie, nor may their spirit be raised as a ghost. A body that lies on solid ground when this charm is used sinks into the ground and the body will not be scavenged by animals. If used against a zombie then it collapses instantly and buries itself. Against more unusual corpse creations roll (Charisma + Medicine) against a difficulty of the creator's (Essence) to destroy them.<br /> <br /> <b>Peaceable Conclusion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Medicine 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Smooth Transition<br /> If Smooth Transition is used to kill someone who was dying of a disease or poison then the Sidereal learns what that poison was and gains +1 non-charm success when treating that specific disease or poison in the future. By using Smooth Transition on the victims of many diseases the Sidereal may build up a catalogue of diseases and poisons which she finds easier to treat.<br /> <br /> <b>Invocation of the Storm Following Violence</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (+3m, 1wp);<b> Mins:</b> Medicine 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Smooth Transition<br /> By paying a surcharge of three motes and one willpower when activating Smooth Transition the Sidereal may affect all those within an area out to short range.<br /> If this charm is used against a zombie battlegroup the Sidereal rolls (Charisma + Medicine) with +(Essence) non-charm successes against a difficulty of the creator's (Essence). Threshold successes on the roll are inflicted as points of magnitude damage on the battlegroup.<br /> <br /> <b>Deferred Wounds</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Medicine 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Stackable, Decisive Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>(Wits + Medicine) hours<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Sidereal can push one level of damage (Wits + Medicine) hours into the future. This effect may be stacked up to (Essence) times, but doing so does not extent the duration, instead all the health levels are deferred until the same point as the first activation of this charm. At the end of the charm all the wounds come back as they were when the charm was activated adding on to existing damage as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Terminate Illness</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m;<b> Mins:</b> Medicine 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Peacable Conclusion<br /> Roll (Intelligence + Medicine) against a difficulty that varies based on how far advanced the target's symptoms are, success cures the target and allows them to begin to recover. If the victim is suffering from minor symptoms then the difficulty is (Virulence), if the victim is suffering from major symptoms then the difficulty is (Virulence + Mortality) and if the victim is suffering from defining symptoms then the difficulty is (Virulence + [2 * Mortality]).<br /> <br /> <b>Earth and Sky Bargain</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Medicine 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Invocation of the Storm Following Violence, Deferred Wounds, Terminate Illness<br /> This charm summons a dying spirit to the Sidereal and offers them a bargain. If they refuse then they die during that scene. If the spirit accepts then their essence is absorbed by the Sidereal who gains +(Essence) soak and an extra [-0] health level. This charm's effects may be passed on to another beneficiary by touching them. When this charm ends the spirit is reborn, slightly changed and no longer on the verge of death.<br /> <hr /> <u><b>Melee</b></u><br /> <b>Meditation on War</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Melee 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Sidereal may convert up to the lower of (Essence) or (Weapon's Accuracy) dice into successes before the attack pool is rolled.<br /> <br /> <b>Impeding the Flow</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Melee 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Increase the target number of an attack targeting the Sidereal by one.<br /> <br /> <b>Harmony of Blows</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Meditation on War<br /> Make up to the lower of Dexterity or 3 <b>decisive</b> attacks. Initiative must be split between them, with a minimum of 3 initiative going into each attack. The attacks may be against one or multiple enemies and may be made using any combat ability. The Sidereal's initiative does not reset until all attacks have been made. This charm may be combined with other abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Smiling at the Damned</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Melee 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only, Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Harmony of Blows<br /> After the raw damage of the attack has been compared to hardness the Sidereal halves the damage pool (round up) and makes any damage dealt Aggravated.<br /> <br /> <b>Serenity in Blood</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Melee 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Impeding the Flow<br /> Double the Sidereal's Parry rating, including weapon bonus but ignoring all penalties, against a single attack. This charm also allows the Sidereal to apply their parry rating against unblockable effects. This charm explicitly allows the Sidereal to break their dice cap, but may not be combined with other charms that add to their Parry rating.<br /> <br /> <b>Perfection of the Visionary Warrior</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Melee 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Smiling at the Damned, Serenity in Blood<br /> While this charm is active unexpected attacks do not reduce the Sidereal's defense against them. Additionally she may make a <b>withering</b> counterattack once per turn using her Melee, Brawl, MA, Archery or Thrown dice pools (assuming she has an appropriate weapon readied).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T03:55:51-08:00","id":790197,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Occult</b></u><br /> <b>Mark of Exaltation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Occult 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Spirits within short range of the Sidereal using this charm become visible to everyone, even if dematerialized. This does not make them any easier to interact with physically however. Additionally the Sidereal gains +1 non-charm success on Occult, Presence, Performance, Bureaucracy and Socialize rolls when dealing with spirits or within Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> <b>Tell Tale Symphony</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> The Sidereal can sense nearby spirits (even if they are immaterial), permanent magical effects/objects and sorcery. A successful (Intelligence + Occult) roll against difficulty 3 allows the Sidereal to identify details about the enchantment or the rank and job of a detected spirit. Alternatively the Sidereal gains details about the local geomantic environment.<br /> <br /> <b>Incite Decorum</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m;<b> Mins:</b> Occult 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Unless the Sidereal is the one to initiate hostilities then the spirit must pay (Essence/2, round up) Willpower in order to roll Join Battle against the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> <b>Innocuous Maneuver</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m;<b> Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Tell Tale Symphony, Incite Decorum<br /> This charm gives the target spirit a positive minor tie towards the Sidereal of the Sidereal's choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Unweaving Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Occult 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only, Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Innocuous Maneuver<br /> A <b>decisive</b> attack targeted with (Perception + Occult) that does not reset the Sidereal's initiative. The attack does (Essence) + threshold successes aggravated damage to a single target within short range. If the target is killed they are completely unmade, their soul not reincarnating. This charm does not affect the dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Willing Assumption of Chains</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Occult 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Unweaving Method<br /> A god signs the prayer strip and is instantly given a new office end responsibilities as decided by the Sidereal. Prudence suggests that the Sidereal pick suitable candidates for new posts. Likewise a prudent god asks what the duty they will be accepting is. This charm only works if the god signs of their own free will and threatening a god to make them sign is a serious crime in Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrestrial Circle Sorcery</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Sidereal steps through the First Circle and is forever transformed. Upon learning this Charm, the Exalt gains the ability to learn and cast spells from the Terrestrial Circle of sorcery. In addition, the Sidereal learns one shaping ritual (p. 466) and one Terrestrial spell for free, the spell selected becomes the sorcerer\u2019s \u201ccontrol spell&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Celestial Circle Sorcery</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Occult 4, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> The Sidereal ascends to the Second Circle and becomes an avatar bearing aspects of Heaven and Hell in her mind. In all the world, there are only a handful of sorcerers at this level of power. Upon learning this Charm, the Exalt gains the ability to cast spells from the Celestial Circle of sorcery. In addition, the Solar learns one shaping ritual and one Celestial spell for free. The spell selected acts as an additional control. <hr /> <u><b>Performance</b></u><br /> <b>Compassionate Essence Replenishment</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Performance 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Whenever the Sidereal successfully influences a large group with Performance she gains (Essence) motes. This bonus may only be received once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Perfection in Life</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m;<b> Mins:</b> Performance 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> When making a performance-based social influence every person whose Resolve is beaten by the social influence roll gains one temporary willpower. This may take someone above their permanent willpower, but excess willpower disappears at the end of the scene. This chamr may only be used once per scene and individuals may only benefit from the bonus willpower once per day.<br /> <br /> <b>Defense of Shining Joy</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Performance 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Perfection in Life<br /> For the duration of the charm the Sidereal only suffers half the effect of onslaught penalties (round down) and gains 1i for every attack that is successfully avoided.<br /> <br /> <b>Song of Spirit Persuasion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Performance 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Perfection in Life<br /> Roll (Manipulation + Performance) against a difficulty of the higher of a spirit's (Resolve) or (Essence). Success on the roll makes the spirit an Ally (as per the Merit) until the end of the story. If treated well the spirit may become a permanent Ally. Spirits of Earth, Water or Air association increase the difficulty of the roll by 2. Usable once per story.<br /> <br /> <b>Faultless Ceremony</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Performance 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> At the end of a ceremony in which the Sidereal participates roll (Manipulation + Performance) against a difficulty of (8 - resources spent on the ceremony). Success on the roll gives all participants in the ceremony a speciality dice on all of their efforts for a week.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart-Brightening Presentation Style</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Performance 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Sidereal may substitute their Bureaucracy, Presence or Socialize with their Performance in any one roll or derived value. This may even be used to roll Performance instead of the associated skill in a charm that requires a specific roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Harmonic Completion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 16m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Performance 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Five days<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Defense of Shining Joy, Song of Spirit Persuasion, Faultless Ceremony, Heart-Brightening Presentation Style<br /> For the duration of the charm the Sidereal becomes blind (as per the flaw). All performance-based social influences inspire love/compassion (Sidereal's choice) in observers on top of their normal effect. The inspire action uses the successes of the social influence roll to determine it's success. Additionally any instill action to create or strengthen an intimacy of love/compassion converts (Essence) dice to successes before rolling. <hr /> <u><b>Presence</b></u><br /> <b>Heroic Essence Replenishment</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Presence 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Whenever the Sidereal successfully influences a large group with Presence she gains (Essence) motes. This bonus may only be received once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Presence in Absence Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Presence 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Stackable<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> This charm may be activated after a successful instill action. The results of the instill action do not come into effect until the Sidereal decides. This means that no-one other than the Sidereal may interact with the 'new/altered' intimacy, not even the target.<br /> This charm may be stacked up to (Essence) times on a target allowing for multiple changes to be made without the subject being aware until the Sidereal decides. This allows for the Sidereal to hide complete reversals in personality until the time of their choosing by creating a new Defining Intimacy and/or degrading existing intimacies before releasing them onto the target later.<br /> <br /> <b>Impose Nature</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Presence 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> If the Intimacy that is being instilled is one that the Sidereal has (at major or defining) then the instilled intimacy counts as being one level lower for the purposes of requiring supporting intimacies.<br /> <br /> <b>Force Decision</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m;<b> Mins:</b> Presence 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Impose Nature<br /> A social influence supplemented with this charm costs an extra willpower to deny/resist.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalty-Sacrificing Sidestep</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Presence 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Presence in Absence Technique<br /> This charm may be activated by the Sidereal after their Resolve has been beaten by a social influence. It allows them to redirect the resolution of the social influence onto someone else present at the scene. The new target of the social influence must have a positive tie towards the Sidereal. In addition to the effects of the social influence one positive tie towards the Sidereal is weakened by one level.<br /> <br /> <b>Vizier's Portentous Advice</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 15m, 1wp 2xp;<b> Mins:</b> Presence 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Force Decision, Loyalty-Sacrificing Sidestep<br /> This charm can be used to permanently enhance a mortal. The mortal gains a personal Essence pool of five motes, the Exalted Healing Merit and gains +1 dot in an Attribute of the Sidereal's choice. If the mortal has Integrity 3+ then they get a charm called Providential Determination which allows them to reflexively spend five motes of Essence instead of a willpower. A Sidereal may enhance up to (Essence), different, mortals at a time and if any mortal dies then the experience spent on them is refunded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":8793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","user":"Grifftofer","date":".  Fixing early morning errors 12-21-2015, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T03:58:17-08:00","id":790198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The Sidereal ascends to the Second Circle and becomes an avatar bearing aspects of Heaven and Hell in her mind. In all the world, there are only a handful of sorcerers at this level of power. Upon learning this Charm, the Exalt gains the ability to cast spells from the Celestial Circle of sorcery. In addition, the <b>Solar</b> learns one shaping ritual and one Celestial spell for free. The spell selected acts as an additional control.&quot; </div> </div> </div>How do you pick which Solar gains the fruit of your efforts, though?<br /> <br /> Not to mention that Sidereals don't even have anima iconography to be affected by the control spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T04:13:19-08:00","id":790204,"title":"","content":"Doh! That'll teach me to try to do things at 2am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T14:50:00-08:00","id":790506,"title":"","content":"So. I know this is a bad idea as I have yet to finish the base trees for this conversion project. But I couldn't help getting some ideas for things that might be fun to include, or to expand the various trees.<br /> <br /> Note that many of the names are WIP or placeholder, several were taken from the wiki (because I thought they sounded good) others I have made up myself. Ideas for cool sounding sidereal charm names will always be welcome, and may spark an idea too. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Archery</u></b><br /> <b>Hawk Feathered Arrow-</b> The arrow turns into a hawk allowing the Sidereal to survey their surroundings through the hawks eyes.<br /> <b>Splitting the Arrow Shot-</b> If crash an opponent may immediately make a decisive follow-up.<br /> <b>Earth Like Air Trick-</b> Allows an attack to be made unexpected with a successful opposed check. The target suffers penalties based on the amount of cover they have from the Sidereal.<br /> <b>Cracked Shell Divinations-</b> Soak piercer that improves at high initiative.<br /> <b>Bolts of Starlight-</b> Supplements an attack allowing the Sidereal to shoot at medium range without aiming.<br /> <b>Arms of the Crimson Panoply-</b> Reflexively make a draw/ready weapon action and for the rest of the scene count as having the Extra Limbs merit. (Have 2 extra hands to hold onto things)<br /> <b>Stinging Incitation Strike-</b> If threshold successes are equal to or greater than target's Resolve, they must make a rush action with you as the target next turn. May be combined with other abilities.<br /> <b>Volley of Legions-</b> Add (Essence) to raw damage of a withering attack. The shot hits everyone within close range of the target. The Sidereal gains initiative based only on the highest damage dealt.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Athletics</u><br /> Sky Touching Toad Technique-</b> The air can support the Sidereal for one turn.<br /> <b>Strength of Five Prana-</b> The Sidereal may increase her strength by up to (Essence). The combined total may not go above 6.<br /> <b>Passing Army Disturbance-</b> May pass through a battlegroup without spending initiative. Battlegroups must roll initiative to successfully Engage her.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Brawl</u><br /> Violet Murder Venom-</b> Coats the Sidereal's attack in a poison. May be combined with other abilities.<br /> <b>Room Emptying Murderer-</b> A fear effect that causes lesser opponents to flee.<br /> <b>Numb as the Dead Technique-</b> Activate to make an attack not reduce the turns of control in a grapple.<br /> <b>Unrelenting Flesh Method-</b> Increase soak/hardness whilst in a grapple.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Craft</u><br /> Inspirational Works Technique-</b> May attach a social influence onto a crafted item. The influence fades over time.<br /> <b>Feathers of Beautiful Seeming-</b> Increase the Sidereal's Appearance by 1.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Dodge</u><br /> Auspicious Reversal-</b> Initiative lost when making unsuccessful decisive attacks against the Sidereal increase the Sidereal's initiative.<br /> <b>Cooperative Defense Technique-</b> Improves defense if the Sidereal and another are both defending each other.<br /> <b>Pursuit of Love-</b> Convert (Intimacy) dice to successes on a rush/disengage roll. The Intimacy must be one of love.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Larceny</u><br /> Words Without Words Deception-</b> Take no penalties to a social influence based on non-verbal communication to communicate a lie or untruth.<br /> <b>Gambler's Den Method-</b> The Sidereal always has a hideout nearby to retreat to.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Linguistics</u><br /> Cunning Editor Reading-</b> Increase Resolve against written social influences.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lore</u><br /> Sifu in the Dojo-</b> When teaching, students are unusually attentive and learn more quickly.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Melee</u><br /> Swift Pressed Attack-</b> A multi attack that applies onslaught penalty for the attacks upfront from the first attack.<br /> <b>Thousand Weapon Training-</b> Reflexively ready/draw a weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T05:07:13-08:00","id":794766,"title":"","content":"So after most of a week off for the holidays, here are two more abilities to look at. Not too many more to go now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /> <u><b>Resistance</b></u><br /> <b>Ox-Body Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Stackable<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The bodies of the Exalted are much more durable than those of mere mortals. To help simulate this, an Exalt may buy extra health levels with this Charm. The purchasing choices are based on the character\u2019s Stamina rating:<br /> - At Stamina 1 and 2: One -1 health level.<br /> - 3 and 4: One -0 health level.<br /> - 5: One -0 and one -1 health level.<br /> The Sidereal may purchase Ox-Body Technique (Resistance) times. If she increases her Stamina after purchasing Ox-Body Technique, her health levels automatically change to reflect the new rating.<br /> <br /> <b>Red Haze</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Ox Body Technique<br /> Gives a single battlegroup of up to Size (Essence), +1 to it's Might when fighting against the Undead, Demons or Fae. The effect can be stacked by multiple Sidereals using this charm on a battlegroup (up to Might 3), but may not be used multiple times on a battlegroup by a single Sidereal.<br /> <br /> <b>Optimistic Security Practice</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous, Withering Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Gain +(Essence) soak and a defensive pool of (Resistance) Initiative for one round. Any <b>withering</b> damage steals these temporary points before spilling over to damage the Sidereal\u2019s own Initiative. They are not added to <b>decisive</b> attacks nor can they be used for any other purpose besides taking <b>withering</b> damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Someone Else's Destiny</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Instead of rolling to resist a poison the Sidereal traps it in a loop of fate. The poison is the applied to her next successful decisive attack, which uses up the poison in her system and ends the charm. Using this charm a second time whilst a poison is already trapped reintroduces the first poison into her system. She must now roll to resist the poison as normal.<br /> At Essence 3+ this charm gains the Stackable keyword. Allowing the Sidereal to use this charm to hold up to (Essence) poisons in limbo at a time. Activating this charm again allows the Sidereal to chose which poison gets reintroduced into her system.<br /> <br /> <b>Shield of Destiny</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m;<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous, Decisive Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Optimistic Security Prana, Someone Else's Destiny<br /> This charm may be activated after damage has been rolled on a <b>decisive </b>attack. Roll (Resistance + Stamina), for every 2 successes on the roll reduce the damage dealt to the Sidereal by the attack by one health level, up to a maximum of the damage dealt by the attack. The damage removed by this charm is then stored and may be used by the Sidereal to enhance a <b>decisive </b>attack. The damage is a separate pool, so isn't added to the pool to determine whether the attack gets past the target's hardness. The held damage pool ignores hardness and has the same damage type as when it was inflicted on the Sidereal. The Sidereal may have up to (Essence) of these held damage pools at a time, but may only use one to enhance a given decisive attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Water and Fire Treaty</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp, 1hl;<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Stackable<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Ox Body Technique<br /> The Sidereal gains +(Resistance) soak and hardness against damage from one elemental source, chosen when the charm is initiated. This charm may be stacked up to (Essence) times, but each use of the charm must chose a different element to protect against.<br /> <br /> <b>Water and Fire Legion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (+2m/person);<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Water and Fire Treaty, Red Haze<br /> By paying a surcharge of two motes per person, the Sidereal may include others in her activation of Water and Fire Treaty. The Sidereal may bestow the benefits on to up to (Essence) others.<br /> <br /> <b>Heartless Maiden Trance</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 4, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Shield of Destiny<br /> The Sidereal halves wound penalties (round down) and may ignore penalties from fatigue, exhaustion and armour. Poisons and diseases pause their effects whilst the charm is active and the Sidereal needs no sleep, food, drink or to breathe. The Sidereal may not be rendered unconscious while this charm is active and does not respire Essence except through charms. When this charm is ended any effects that where paused, ignored or added to the Sidereal during the charm kick in at the point they were at when she activated the charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm's Eye Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Resistance 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip, Dual<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Heartless Maiden Trance, Water and Fire Legion<br /> The Sidereal may launch counterattacks against up to (Essence) targets for 2 motes per target. A battlegroup may be targeted up to (Size) times by a single counterattack. The counterattack type is the same as the attack which it is countering and has a base damage equal to that of the attack the Sidereal is countering. Extra successes do not add to the base damage of <b>withering</b> attacks and the Sidereal's initiative is not factored into the damage of <b>decisive</b> attacks. A <b>decisive</b> counterattack created by this charm does not reset the Sidereal's initiative.<br /> <hr /> <u><b>Ride</b></u><br /> <b>Ordained Bridle of Mercury</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Ride 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> This charm summons a creature from the area to become the Sidereal's Familiar. The creature summoned is a two-dot Familiar and is usually a riding creature of some kind. By spending a surcharge of +1 willpower the player may choose the species of the new Familiar.<br /> <br /> <b>Breaking the Wild Mortal</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Ride 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Ordained Bridle of Mercury<br /> The Sidereal gains a dot in the Acquaintances merit for this area. This increase fades at the end of the story unless the Sidereal makes an effort to maintain the connection.<br /> <br /> <b>Yellow Path</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m;<b> Mins:</b> Ride 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The shortest path to the Sidereal's destination is illuminated by a glimmering yellow light. The path is not necessarily safe, but all obstacles on the way should be surmountable by the Sidereal. The charm takes into account all delays such as from difficult terrain, stopping for food/rest and recovering from injuries. Roll (Essence), one success give a substantial improvement over the normal travel time between start and end points. If the Sidereal has a deadline then 3 successes indicates a timely arrival and 5 allows the Sidereal to make any appointment she has not already missed.<br /> <br /> <b>Glory Path</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m;<b> Mins:</b> Ride 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Yellow Path<br /> Add one to a mount's Speed. The mount may also ignore penalties to movement for natural obstacles/barriers. Artificial obstacles/barriers effect the Sidereal and her mount as normal. The Sidereal's mount is even able to run up the sides of cliff faces or across bodies of water.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Shape Companion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp, 2xp;<b> Mins:</b> Ride 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Ordained Bridle of Mercury<br /> A Familiar enhanced by this charm becomes an Essence 1 minor god. The Familiar gains a mote pool appropriate to a god of it's Essence and the Materialize charm. (It may gain other charms as deemed appropriate by the ST.) It's Intelligence also increases to 2, if it is not already higher. Finally the Familiar gains a number of additional [-0] health levels equal to it's (Essence). Yu-Shan becomes aware of this new god and registers it in their archives. The god's primary duty is to provide service to the character, but it may be reassigned if necessary. If the Familiar is killed or reassigned any experience invested into it is returned to the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> <b>Godly Companion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 20m, 1wp, 5xp;<b> Mins:</b> Ride 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Spirit Shape Companion<br /> The Familiar's Essence increases by one to a maximum of the Sidereal's Essence. It's Intelligence increases to a minimum of 3 and it learns at least 2 additional charms. The Familiar now has an innate ability to travel between Creation and Yu-Shan along with up to (Essence) others. The more powerful the Familiar becomes the greater the chance of it being assigned additional duties or being reassigned from the Sidereal altogether. This charm may only be used once per story.<br /> <br /> <b>Riding the Dragon</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 20m, 1wp, 1hl;<b> Mins:</b> Ride 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Breaking the Wild Mortal, Glory Path, Godly Companion<br /> Once activated this charm turns an Acquaintance or Familiar temporarily into a Lesser Elemental Dragon. This transformation takes 5 turns and is extremely painful to endure. Once the charm ends the creature returns to it's original state, but as a burned-out husk. Able to accept food and mumble incoherently, but nothing more. A Familiar is now completely unfit for the purpose and thus that merit is permanently lost, but an Acquaintance rating is reduced or lost depending on individual's importance to the merit (As determined by the ST).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T05:20:32-08:00","id":794770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=782504#post782504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's completely understandable. Just don't list &amp;quot;Having very few amount of high essence charms&amp;quot; as a design feature of your Ex3 Sidereal update. It makes me irrationally scared that the developers will get the idea to do the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no you fool! Leave it in! I'm pretty sure that it's a developer rule never to include home brew as an inspiration for actual mechanics. It pollutes the integrity of the game line or something.<br /> <br /> Also sorry I'm so late to this party, I haven't read the whole thread yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T06:15:39-08:00","id":794784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=794766#post794766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Riding the Dragon</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You're removing the ability to leave them a Dragon permanently? That was one of the coolest bits about it in my book. I'd have suggested that you instead pay XP to upgrade them to a 5-dot Ally.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T06:33:19-08:00","id":794792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=794770#post794770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no you fool! Leave it in! I'm pretty sure that it's a developer rule never to include home brew as an inspiration for actual mechanics. It pollutes the integrity of the game line or something.<br /> <br /> Also sorry I'm so late to this party, I haven't read the whole thread yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe. Maybe you're right. I would be amused if that actually did happen :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=794784#post794784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're removing the ability to leave them a Dragon permanently? That was one of the coolest bits about it in my book. I'd have suggested that you instead pay XP to upgrade them to a 5-dot Ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually only an option that was added in 2nd edition. I do sort of see your point, but the idea for me of the charm is about Sidereals having to make terrible decisions that may wreck the fate of an individual in order to save the world (Needs of the many kind of thing). I might add back in the option to keep them as an elemental dragon, but I probably won't make them an Ally. More likely I'd make it so that the Sidereal may pay &quot;cost&quot; to keep them in that form, but the memory of the pain leaves the new dragon indisposed towards the Sidereal (Major Intimacy of distrust/dislike?). Then there would be a bit of a moral choice to make. You can give the acquaintance/familiar a new life, but you may make them a potential antagonist to work around. Or you leave them to their fate, but have to live with the fact that you made them that way, discarding their individuality and potential for the sake of the greater good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T17:21:35-08:00","id":795213,"title":"","content":"A thoroughly productive afternoon and evening later and I've finished pass one of the Sidereal charmset. Yay! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll look at making any minor changes that have been suggested here and putting a document up to make it easier to read through in the morning. Any and all comments are welcome as usual. And enjoy. <hr /> <u><b>Sail</b></u><br /> <b>Stone Skipping Spirit</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Sail 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Pilot<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Sidereal may allow her ship to ignore any penalties to a sail roll, based on weather, dangers or other environmental factors.<br /> <br /> <b>Serendipitous Voyage</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Sail 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One journey<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Sidereal is able to find transport to any destination. Even if the captain does not intend that as the destination, the Sidereal's fate will lead her to arrive there.<br /> <br /> <b>Salt Into Ash Sleight</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Sail 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> A targeted spirit/elemental/creature of the sea gains a minor intimacy towards leaving and being elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <b>Mirror Shattering Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m (+1wp);<b> Mins:</b> Sail 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Pilot<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Stone Skipping Method<br /> The ship, crew and Sidereal become partially dematerialized. Checks to spot the ship are made at a -2 penalty, the ship gains +1 speed and can travel over land without penalty. However those aboard ship cannot see Creation around them and suffer a -3 penalty to any rolls to navigate whilst the charm is active. If the Sidereal leaves the ship or is killed this charm ends immediately with the ship returning to Creation fully, this could put the ship somewhere on land if it has been navigated incorrectly.<br /> Alternatively the Sidereal may sail from Creation to the ports of Yu-Shan, a journey that takes five days. It may be possible to travel to Malfeas or the Underworld through use of this charm, but if so the paths have been kept secret.<br /> This charm may be activated even if the Sidereal does not have a vessel to travel on, at a surcharge of +1 willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Walls of Salt and Ash</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m/Hull, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Sail 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Salt Into Ash Sleight<br /> For every 4m spent the ship the Sidereal is on gains a [-0] Hull level. A Sidereal may only add up to her (Essence) in Hull levels to a ship<br /> <br /> <b>Creation Smuggling Procedures</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Sail 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Pilot<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One day<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> This charm protects the Sidereal and her vessel and crew against the environmental warping effects of the Wyld. The direct actions of creatures of the Wyld may still affect/damage her or the ship, but the general influence of the Wyld does not. This charm may be activated whilst not on a ship, in which case it protects those within close range of the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> <b>Five Ordeals Odyssey</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 15m, 1wp, llhl;<b> Mins:</b> Sail 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Serendipitous Voyage, Mirror Shattering Method, Walls of Salt and Ash, Creation Smuggling Procedures<br /> If, while this charm is active, a dangerous opponent is about to recover to base Initiative having been crashed for 3 turns this charm automatically ends their threat (albeit, potentially temporarily). The ST describes the way in which the opponent has been driven off/incapacitated/ killed, so recurring villains may well survive to blight the Sidereal again. This charm may be used once per story.<br /> <hr /> <u><b>Socialize</b></u><br /> <b>Stern Essence Replenishment</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -;<b> Mins:</b> Socialize 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Whenever the Sidereal successfully influences a large group with Socialize she gains (Essence) motes. This bonus may only be received once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Shun the Smiling Lady</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Socialize 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The target's Appearance is reduced by 1 and any attempts to seduce someone counts as being opposed by a defining intimacy. By paying a surcharge of five motes the duration of this charm may be extended to Indefinite. If this version of the charm is used then the target's Appearance continues to drop over the next week until it reaches 1. At which point any Intimacies of romance, love or lust towards her begin to degrade. Intimacies degrade at a rate of one level per week. If this charm is ended then Appearance loss recovers over the next week back to it's original value, but any degradation of Intimacies is permanent.<br /> <br /> <b>Cash and Murder Games</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m;<b> Mins:</b> Socialize 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Shun the Smiling Lady<br /> The target gains a minor positive Intimacy towards someone of the Sidereal's choice. The Sidereal may not be the beneficiary of this Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Life Without Compunction</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Socialize 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Roll (Manipulation + Socialize) against the target's resolve in order to make them ignore a social violation or taboo. 3 threshold successes instills a minor positive intimacy in the target towards the rule-breaker. 5 threshold successes makes the taboo that the person broke socially acceptable to the target. This charm does not affect any of the legal consequences that may arise from causing a violation or breaking the taboo.<br /> <br /> <b>You and Yours Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Socialize 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Life Without Compunction<br /> If the Sidereal's Socialize &gt; Resolve then roll (Willpower) against a difficulty of (Essence). Failure means that the opponent may not attack the character. The roll may be re-attempted as an action, which may be flurried as normal. The Sidereal also gains +(Essence) successes on seduction rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Fortuitous Fellowship</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 12m;<b> Mins:</b> Socialize 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One week<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Fortuitous Fellowship<br /> The Sidereal spends a week creating and gathering members for a new social group. Roll (Wits + Socialize) with each success increasing the Size of the group created by one. Successes beyond five force the group to expand beyond the area in which the Sidereal is working, starting again from Size zero and increasing by one per success.<br /> The Sidereal defines the policies for the group, but not which specific individuals will join. Once the charm ends the group operates on its own, unless the Sidereal made herself (or a Resplendent Destiny, the groups leader. From then on it's policies and survival are based on the groups own merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Wanting and Fearing Prayer</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Socialize 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinte<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Fortuitous Fellowship, Cash and Murder Games<br /> Roll (Manipulation + Socialize) against the Resolve of two people who must be in line of sight of the Sidereal when activating this charm. If the Sidereal successfully beasts both of the targets' Resolves then she may define a social relationship between them. Both targets gain a major intimacy towards one another that is appropriate to the social relationship created. As long as the essence is committed the Intimacy created is protected from being weakened.<br /> The targets may spend 1 willpower to act contrary to the created Intimacy for a scene. Once either has spent (Essence) willpower in this way they break free of this charm. If the targets break free or the charm is ended then the protection of the Intimacy ends and it may be eroded as normal. Additionally the social relationship ceases to exist.<br /> <hr /> <b><u>Stealth</u></b><br /> <b>Soft Presence Practice</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m;<b> Mins:</b> Stealth 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Half the number of motes of Peripheral Essence spent for the purposes of adding to the Sidereal's anima banner, rounding down.<br /> <br /> <b>Walking Outside Fate</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Stealth 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Soft Presence Practice<br /> The character steps outside of Fate, attempts to perceive or track her suffer a -3 penalty. Additionally attacks made by those with an Initiative 5+ points lower than the Sidereal suffer this penalty to their attack rolls.<br /> If the Sidereal's anima banner reaches the Burning level then this charm ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Subordinate Inspiration Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Stealth 4, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Walking Outside Fate<br /> Whilst Walking Outside Fate is active the Sidereal may use this charm to talk directly into a spirit's mind. The target spirit rolls (Wits + Awareness) against a difficulty of the Sidereal's (Essence). Failure means that the spirit counts as Resolve 0 against the influence (though they may increase this with Intimacies as normal). Success means that they only suffer a -2 penalty to their Resolve.<br /> If this charm is simply used to hold a conversation, and not to transmit a social influence, then it's duration is extended to 5 minutes.<br /> <br /> <b>Blinding the Boar</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Stealth 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Soft Presence Practice<br /> Become indistinct and blurry, raising the target number of any (Perception + Awareness) roll opposing stealth by 1, and lower penalties on Stealth rolls by 2. Enemies with an Initiative 5+ points lower than the Sidereal also suffer an increased target number on attacks against her.<br /> <br /> <b>Gift of the Broken Mask</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp +2m/day;<b> Mins:</b> Stealth 3, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Up to one week<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Blinding the Boar<br /> Roll (Dexterity + Stealth) against a difficulty of the target's (Essence). Success places the victim under the vagaries of Arcane Fate, exactly as a Sidereal is. Additionally the target becomes immune to the Arcane Fate of others whilst under the effects of this charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Ceasing to Exist Approach</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 2wp (+5m);<b> Mins:</b> Stealth 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Subordinate Inspiration Technique, Gift of the Broken Mask<br /> The Sidereal disappears from her current location and reappears somewhere else in a completely different identity, which is seamlessly integrated into the local community. The identity created is completely new and not that of someone already extant in Creation.<br /> The ST determines where the Sidereal reappears, but the character may decide an appropriate identity for the location. In her new identity she retains Attribute and Ability dots, but gains up to 15 points of Merits appropriate to her new identity. Dots over 3 cost two points each.<br /> The character retains all Charms, Spells and anima powers. If the character's new identity is of an Exalt then observers understand the Sidereal's powers as being appropriate to an Exalt of the type she is supposed to be. The character never suffers penalties to social influences, for outlandish claims, to convince people of things relating to her new identity.<br /> Only creatures that are outside of fate, or above the level of power of the Maidens, can tell that the character's new identity wasn't always part of the location.<br /> This charm ends if ever the Sidereal's anima banner reaches the Burning level. The effects of the charm linger for 5 days after which the Sidereal resumes her previous identity and reappears in the place that identity calls home.<br /> For a surcharge of five motes this charm may be activated reflexively in response to an attack that strikes her whilst she is crashed, or an attack that causes her to be crashed.<br /> <hr /> <u><b>Survival</b></u><br /> <b>Becoming the Wilderness</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Survival 1, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One day<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Animals with Resolve &lt; Sidereal's Survival will ignore the Sidereal as a non-threat, so long as she doesn't attack or attempt to steal from them.<br /> <br /> <b>Adopting the Untamed Face</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Survival 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One hour<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Becoming the Wilderness<br /> The Sidereal can communicate with a single species of wild animal, allowing her to attempt social influence rolls against them. If (Essence) is equal to or greater than the animal's (Resolve) then they also gain a minor intimacy of respect towards the Sidereal<br /> <br /> <b>Dreaming the Wild Lands</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m;<b> Mins:</b> Survival 4, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Becoming the Wilderness<br /> The Sidereal may make cosmetic changes to the landscape out to extreme range, equivalent to those that could be made by a team of mortal workers over a period of (Essence) weeks. Lunars interacting with the Sidereal in a scene in which this charm has been activated temporarily gain a minor tie of respect towards her.<br /> <br /> <b>Sky and Rain Mantra</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m;<b> Mins:</b> Survival 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One day<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Becoming the Wilderness<br /> Roll (Stamina + Survival) each success allows the Sidereal to inflict a one dice penalty or add one non-charm dice to the Survival rolls of everyone within (Essence) miles. If two characters use this charm such that their areas overlap then the roll becomes contested.<br /> <br /> <b>Sky Spirit Demand</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Survival 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sky and Rain Mantra<br /> The Sidereal counts as though she had succeeded at two instill actions if she succeeds with an instill action against a spirit supplemented by this charm. If this charm is used against a spirit of an elemental affinity other than air then they gain +1 Resolve against the action for every point of (Essence) they are greater than the Sidereal (minimum of +1).<br /> <br /> <b>Wilderness-Commanding Practice</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> Survival 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Five days<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Adopting the Untamed Face, Dreaming the Wild Lands, Sky Spirit Demand<br /> So long as the Sidereal can see her prayer strip she can use Adopting the Untamed Face to communicate with animals she cannot see, so long as they are within (Essence) miles of the prayer strip. Additionally she may commit two motes per person to grant them +3 successes on Survival rolls or to increase the difficulty of their Survival rolls by 3, so long as they are within the same area. Once this charm is activated the prayer strip may not be moved from its location.<br /> <hr /> <u><b>Thrown</b></u><br /> <b>Willful Weapon Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Thrown 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The onslaught penalty inflicted by this attack does not fade for (Essence) turns.<br /> <br /> <b>Life Gets Worse Approach</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Thrown 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Willful Weapon Method<br /> Add one success to the <b>decisive</b> damage roll. For the rest of the scene the Sidereal may spend two motes to redirect a ranged attack that misses it's target, so long as the target is within close range of the victim. The attack uses the same attack roll as the original attack, but with up to (Thrown) non-successes re-rolled. If a <b>withering</b> attack is redirected into the victim then the damage roll does not give initiative to either the Sidereal or the original attacker, instead the initiative is simply lost. A <b>decisive</b> attack that is redirected likewise does not reset the attacker's initiative.<br /> After the Sidereal has redirected (Essence) attacks in this manner the effect fades.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence Thorn Practice</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> Thrown 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Willful Weapon Method<br /> Creates an attack with a summoned Mortal Medium Thrown weapon with the Lethal, Mounted and Thrown (Medium) tags. If the attack hits then the Sidereal is pulled one range band towards the target, even if they have already moved.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Piercing Needle</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m;<b> Mins:</b> Thrown 4, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Essence Thorn Practice<br /> Subtract (Stealth) from the target's armoured soak. If the attack is unexpected, double the amount of soak ignored.<br /> <br /> <b>Pain Amplification Strategem</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m;<b> Mins:</b> Thrown 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Life Gets Worse Approach<br /> The attack gains non-charm dice on it's attack roll equal to the number in the target's wound penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Unrelenting Torment Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Thrown 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive Only, Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Shadow Piercing Needle, Pain Amplification Strategy<br /> A Thrown attack that may be made out to extreme range without aiming. If the attack deals any damage then the Sidereal heals a number of health levels of damage equal to those inflicted. Any target successfully hit with this attack gains a minor intimacy of hatred towards the Sidereal.<br /> <hr /> <u><b>War</b></u><br /> <b>Predestined Triumph Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m/TN reduction;<b> Mins:</b> War 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> When using a Command action on a battlegroup this charm reduces the target number of the battlegroup's actions for this turn by one. This charm may be used up to (Essence) times on a single action, each reducing the target number by one, to a minimum of 4.<br /> <br /> <b>Auspicious Recruitment Drive</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m;<b> Mins:</b> War 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Special<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Predestined Triumph Method<br /> Halves the amount of time to recruit troops for an battlegroup. Normally it takes one day per point of current Size or half a day to get to Size one (Assuming a viable population to draw from). This is for poor Drill troops, it takes twice as long to recruit average Drill troops. Elite Drill Troops may not be recruited, they must be trained.<br /> <br /> <b>Training Mandate of Auspicious Battle</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> War 4, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Five days<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Auspicious Recruitment Drive<br /> A battlegroup of up to (Essence) Size increases their drill rating by one level.<br /> <br /> <b>Training Mandate of Celestial Empowerment</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1xp;<b> Mins:</b> War 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Training Mandate of Auspicious Battle<br /> At the end of a week of training a battlegroup the Sidereal may permanently enhance them. Any time the battlegroup is targeted by a positive astrological effect reduce the effective Scope of the effect by (Essence/2, round down). The essence for this charm is only committed for the training period of one week.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence Draining Battle Pattern</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m;<b> Mins:</b> War 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Predestined Triumph Method<br /> If the Sidereal wins the contested Strategic Maneuver roll then she may activate this charm instead of using a implementing a Stratagem. For every two threshold successes on the roll the enemy increases the costs of any charms activated during the battle by one mote. Up to a maximum of +(Essence) motes or double the charm's cost, whichever is lower.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon Blocking Battle Pattern</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m;<b> Mins:</b> War 5, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Essence Draining Battle Pattern<br /> If the Sidereal wins the contested Strategic Maneuver roll then she may activate this charm instead of using a implementing a Stratagem. For every two successes opponents that are denizens of Malfeas or the Underworld suffer a -1 penalty to dice rolls during the battle. Up to a maximum of -(Essence) dice.<br /> <br /> <b>Training Mandate of War-God Puissance</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 15m, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> War 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One story<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Training Mandate of Celestial Empowerment<br /> At the end of a week of training a battlegroup of spirits may temporarily increase their Essence by one. The spirits also gain two war-related charms as determined by the ST. The benefits last for one story, after which the spirits return to normal. The spirits may not attempt to learn charms for which they do not normally meet the minimum traits for. The maximum size of battlegroup that can be affected by this charm is (Essence/2, round up). The essence for this charm is only committed for the training period of one week.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit-Binding Battle Pattern</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 15m, 1wp, 1lhl;<b> Mins:</b> War 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Demon Blocking Battle Pattern, Training Mandate of War-God Puissance<br /> If the Sidereal wins the contested Strategic Maneuver roll then she may activate this charm instead of using a implementing a Strategem. This allows the Sidereal to summon a named spirit during the battle.<br /> The spirit may have a maximum Essence of the lowest of: 3 + Size of all units on the Sidereal's side; Threshold successes on the Strategic Maneuver roll; 10.<br /> A successful control roll against a difficulty of the spirit's (Essence + Resolve) allows the Sidereal to set the spirit a single task to complete, or have the spirit serve them for a year and a day. If the task option is chosen the spirit is forbidden from attempting to look for revenge against the Sidereal, but not for the year and a day of service.<br /> The dice pool for the control roll starts at zero dice with one being added to the pool for every point of magnitude that the Sidereal's side loses. Once the Sidereal decides they have enough dice to attempt the control roll the actual summoning requires a simple action to accomplish.<br /> Summoning spirits of Essence 4+ is serious matter and the action is always investigated by the Bureau of Fate.<br /> <hr /> <u><b>Martial Arts</b></u><br /> <b>Perfected Lotus Root Mastery</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None;<b> Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Any) 5, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Any one Martial Arts Form charm<br /> The Sidereal may use the <b>Mastery</b> effects for Martial Arts Charms with that keyword.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lotus Bulb Blossoms</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None;<b> Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Any) 5, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Any one complete Martial Arts style, Perfected Lotus Mastery<br /> The Sidereal is capable of discerning that she is in the presence of a spirit, or exalt. The Sidereal may not necessarily know who is the spirit or mortal without further investigation. Practice and experience may allow the Sidereal to tell the difference between exalts, demons, gods and fair folk. This does not let the Sidereal determine between different types of Exalt. They merely know that <u>an Exalt</u> is nearby, not of which god.<br /> Knowing this charm also allows the Sidereal to begin learning Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <b>Transcendent Lotus Understanding</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None;<b> Mins:</b> Martial Arts (Any) 5, Essence 4; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Any one complete Sidereal Martial Arts style, The Lotus Bulb Blossoms<br /> The Sidereal may use <b>Sutra</b> effects for Martial Arts Charms with that keyword.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T04:56:26-08:00","id":796782,"title":"","content":"Ok. So the very first draft of the Document is now available for reading and comments.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Version 1.0</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T06:24:15-08:00","id":796802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=796782#post796782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. So the very first draft of the Document is now available for reading and comments.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Version 1.0</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is awesome. I will start rolling up a character (Chosen of Endings I gave SoulGambit for their WhiteElephant) to test out the rules when I get time.<br /> <br /> Two things I have seen so far:<br /> <br /> One, Solar Experience should be renamed to &quot;Sidereal Experience&quot;. <br /> <br /> Two, considering the Chosen of Secrets Anima Ability involves Guile, Socialize should be added to their list of Caste ability choices. Though, I am unsure which ability to drop. Thrown would be my first choice, but that would leave Secrets without a Caste combat ability. However, since all Sidereals have MA as a favored ability, this might not be as big of a deal as with other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T06:38:45-08:00","id":796808,"title":"","content":"Both good points. I was going to leave it as Solar Experience so that it was obvious how to earn it etc. But a couple of sentences added fixes that issue.<br /> <br /> I can't believe that I never noticed that Socialize wasn't in the Secrets Auspicious Abilitiy list. That has been fixed too, went with the suggestion of swapping out Thrown too, as I agree it is the best option to remove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T06:40:00-08:00","id":796809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=796808#post796808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe that I never noticed that Socialize wasn't in the Secrets Auspicious Abilitiy list. That has been fixed too, went with the suggestion of swapping out Thrown too, as I agree it is the best option to remove.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't notice it either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T06:53:20-08:00","id":796814,"title":"","content":"Do Sidereals get a Supernal Ability in this adaptation? If so, you may want to have Martial Arts be a Caste Ability for all Sidereals, instead of a Favored one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T06:58:47-08:00","id":796815,"title":"","content":"I'm not intending for them to. It seems to be the intent that it be a very 'Solar' thing to be able to excel so completely in a specific area right from the beginning.<br /> <br /> I also feel that there is less of a need for it due to there being so many fewer charms (~170) than the Core and they are all in the Essence 1-3 range (excepting the SMAs I stuck in at the end :P).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T07:03:17-08:00","id":796819,"title":"","content":"The developers hinted somewhere (I think) that other splats are not getting the choice of Supernal ability. I hope that means that other splats don't have to get dumbed down charms. The reason why Solars are so scary is that they get Essence five charms right out of the gate, not because of the charms themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T07:06:01-08:00","id":796822,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping at least Abyssals get something similar, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T07:11:20-08:00","id":796830,"title":"","content":"I feel like they don't really a Supernal Abiility - it's not really part of the Sidereal thing to necessarily be &quot;Every Sidereal is potentially at the peak of Sidereal might at *something*&quot;, rather than grow into their power more generally.<br /> <br /> Plus each Sidereal Ability is relatively fairly narrow and limited in Charms (compared to Solars, even if they end up larger than Grifftofer's conversion), so adding a Supernal Ability onto that would mean they'd have this one Ability they could pull out the Prayer Strip and powerful Charms for.... I feel like you'd rather want to encourage them to pick up Charms in a lot of separate Abilities, with more diversity, since the diversity to each Ability is probably going to be lower.<br /> <br /> As a balance point it also means that low level Sidereal Charms can generally be stronger, since the Solars have Supernal to help them pull ahead (so have less need for generally stronger Charms). It's easier to add a Supernal Ability into a Sidereal game if you feel they need more oomph than to rebalance a lot of Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T08:19:24-08:00","id":796844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=796819#post796819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The developers hinted somewhere (I think) that other splats are not getting the choice of Supernal ability. I hope that means that other splats don't have to get dumbed down charms. The reason why Solars are so scary is that they get Essence five charms right out of the gate, not because of the charms themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect there won't be much of a problem with &quot;this Lunar Charm can't add +3 to [task], because there is a similar Solar Charm that only gives +2&quot;, or &quot;There is a solar Charm that does this too, so this Terrestrial one needs to be more limited&quot; but, taken as a whole, Solar Charms will still probably be mightier in most circumstances. Of course, Martial arts need that sort of thing because everybody uses the same Charms.<br /> <br /> A solar with 6 essence 1 combat Charms probably has a good edge against a Dragon Blooded with also 6 essence 1 Combat Charms and similar stats and equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T10:02:49-08:00","id":796875,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling the way Sids can learn MA Charms is going to be remarkably similar to how a Solar with Supernal MA can learn them, even if the rule governing that won't be called &quot;Supernal Ability&quot;. It'd really steal their thunder as Creation's premier martial artists (which is apparently still a thing of theirs) if a Solar could start the game with full knowledge of a MA Style while they couldn't even get to the Form of some Styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T11:06:54-08:00","id":796913,"title":"","content":"The only thing with that, if there's like, Supernal for Sidereals but only for MA, on the negative side, that seems like it might introduce more weird asymmetries in Sidereal who focus on MA vs other forms of combat and abilities (if that's even meant to be a choice that Sidereals have, between the two, going forward). Another similar example might be how they're supposed to be the premier predictionists as well, and Solar Lore Supernal exists (so do they get an early boost to prediction just so they won't be outdone in predictions by a Lore Supernal Solar at chargen?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:07:51-08:00","id":796939,"title":"","content":"A comment that Sandact6 made on the document has made me think. Do people think that Sifu is worth having as a Merit in a paradigm where Mentor allows someone to learn almost anything they could wish? I guess I thought that Mentor covered the mundane 'stuff' where Sifu could cover the supernatural martial arts, but Mentor covers both.<br /> <br /> So should I just take it out? Or maybe make it so that it is only needed to learn SMAs as a small gating mechanic to show you searching for a willing tutor of the particular style you want to learn? Honestly I'm not too sure. Any thoughts on the matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:59:07-08:00","id":796984,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd just go with Mentor. Adding Sifu feels like unnecessary merit bloat to me since, as you said, Mentor already covers teaching MA","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:48:19-08:00","id":797129,"title":"","content":"While Supernal Ability for Sidereals is certainly too much, I could definitely see a Sid Charm that allows them to early qualify for martial arts charms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:04:34-08:00","id":797963,"title":"","content":"So Sifu has been taken out and it was also pointed out that I had somehow completely neglected to copy over the Awareness charms. Something I totally hadn't noticed :S so those are now in there too for those who haven't seen them.<br /> <br /> Version 1.1 is being worked on at the moment and will have Sidereal Astrology and possibly another SMA or two, if I find time. I hope to be able to get it up within the next week, so are there any thoughts on other essential things to include?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T00:38:05-08:00","id":802902,"title":"","content":"Ok. So <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Version 1.1</a> is now up. It has basic Astrology resolution (no Resplendent Effects just yet) and another couple of SMA styles (Charcoal March of Spiders and Scarlet Patterned Battlefield). There have also been a few minor updates to a couple of charms. Though I think the only one to have changed in actual effect is Elemental Vision.<br /> <br /> Oh and I'd like to thank Scaenicus for his ideas on astrology as they helped me to refine my own. Hopefully you don't feel I've taken too many liberties in using your work as a starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T06:28:49-08:00","id":803027,"title":"","content":"I did a quick read though. The only thing that stood out is that the roll for retaining memories of a Sidereal is usually (Wits + Integrity) -3 instead of (Wits + Occult) - 3.<br /> <br /> I'll have to read the rest later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T06:47:58-08:00","id":803047,"title":"","content":"Yep. That was due to me reading the 1st Ed rules for Arcane Fate. It's been my preference where there are effects that basically were copy-pasted, so I'd forgotten that change. Fixed it now though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T07:07:48-08:00","id":803064,"title":"","content":"This is fantastic. Cant wait to see how it all pulls together once you get Resplendent working","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T07:26:14-08:00","id":803071,"title":"","content":"Glad you like it.<br /> <br /> Resplendent Effects should come over the next week or so I suspect. The building process is there already though, so you can make them. You just have no way to spend your Endurance (Which I guess if half the point of having a resplendent destiny :P). Also been having a bit of a read through the effects this afternoon trying to get ideas for power level and how much a single endurance is worth (compared to essence/willpower).<br /> <br /> The problem is I keep getting distracted by things like interesting looking SMAs or possible new charms to add in. It's proving difficult to keep my focus on the essentials, which is part of the reason this wasn't released earlier in the week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:45:43-08:00","id":803369,"title":"","content":"Are colleges and auspicious abilities and how they connect every explained in the doc? I cant seem to track them down. Also the caste must buy ability dots. Are those given or do they come from your 14 at character creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T03:20:32-08:00","id":803644,"title":"","content":"The colleges/auspicious abilities/astrological houses interplay hasn't been written out yet as I'm not sure where it should go, or whether I'm going stick with the distribution of colleges as they exist currently. For the ability dots it's supposed to read that you get the 6 dots for 'caste' abilities in addition to the 14 you have free reign over. I'll check it and re-write it to make it clearer, probably when I get back after the weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T17:18:56-08:00","id":804131,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be a good idea to make all Sidereal combat Charms cross-applicable with Martial Arts that use the same weapons. It'd solidify the sense of them being the &quot;martial artist Exalted&quot; and it'd make it less of a feel-bad moment when you reach the end of the Melee tree. Switching to a new combat ability is a lot more pleasant if you can keep using your old Charms.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not so sure about some of those Caste Abilities. I think another combat ability would suit Battles better than Lore. And I dunno about the thematics of the Thrown, Presence, and Bureaucracy Charms in Secrets, Serenity, and Journeys.<br /> <br /> I think Sidereals might actually work best with rigid Caste abilities. They've got structured powers and well-defined colleges, after all.<br /> <br /> But if you really want a 5-of-7 setup, how about<br /> <br /> <b>Journeys:</b> Athletics, Dodge, Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival &amp; Thrown.<br /> <b>Serenity:</b> Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Medicine, Performance, Presence &amp; Socialize<br /> <b>Battles:</b> Archery, Athletics, Brawl, Melee, Presence, Resistance &amp; War<br /> <b>Secrets:</b> Integrity, Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth &amp; Thrown<br /> <b>Endings:</b> Awareness, Brawl, Bureaucracy, Integrity, Medicine, Occult &amp; Stealth<br /> <br /> Dodge for Journeys because it's all about being somewhere else. Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme is super-Journeys. Brawl for battles because, well, it's a combat Charmset. And I couldn't think of anything to replace Presence with in Serenity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:44:35-08:00","id":806008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=804131#post804131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'd be a good idea to make all Sidereal combat Charms cross-applicable with Martial Arts that use the same weapons. It'd solidify the sense of them being the &quot;martial artist Exalted&quot; and it'd make it less of a feel-bad moment when you reach the end of the Melee tree. Switching to a new combat ability is a lot more pleasant if you can keep using your old Charms.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not so sure about some of those Caste Abilities. I think another combat ability would suit Battles better than Lore. And I dunno about the thematics of the Thrown, Presence, and Bureaucracy Charms in Secrets, Serenity, and Journeys.<br /> <br /> I think Sidereals might actually work best with rigid Caste abilities. They've got structured powers and well-defined colleges, after all.<br /> <br /> But if you really want a 5-of-7 setup, how about<br /> <br /> <b>Journeys:</b> Athletics, Dodge, Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival &amp; Thrown.<br /> <b>Serenity:</b> Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Medicine, Performance, Presence &amp; Socialize<br /> <b>Battles:</b> Archery, Athletics, Brawl, Melee, Presence, Resistance &amp; War<br /> <b>Secrets:</b> Integrity, Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth &amp; Thrown<br /> <b>Endings:</b> Awareness, Brawl, Bureaucracy, Integrity, Medicine, Occult &amp; Stealth<br /> <br /> Dodge for Journeys because it's all about being somewhere else. Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme is super-Journeys. Brawl for battles because, well, it's a combat Charmset. And I couldn't think of anything to replace Presence with in Serenity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of allowing martial arts to mix with Sidereal charms of an appropriate type is an interesting one. I think it would be ok off the top of my head, but I'd want to have a look at some combinations before I say definitively. Maybe make it a keyword that allows specific charms to cross over?<br /> <br /> Actually that pairs up somewhat with an idea I had to allow Sidereals to cross-apply certain charms from different combat abilities together. So because they are about changing circumstance rather than excellence they might be better able to use existing knowledge in a parallel way. Not sure whether it would homogenise things too much and detract from the uniqueness of the different styles of play.<br /> <br /> I like your ability spread for the castes. I'm not set on the idea of having 7 abilities to pick from for each caste I just thought I'd put it forward and see what people said. I agree that Sids should probably be more structured in terms of their castes than Solars though. I might make some changes to the abilities based on your suggestions, probably not all of them though, as I'm rather attached to the Secrets caste having Socialize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:49:54-08:00","id":806012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=804131#post804131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Journeys:</b> Athletics, Dodge, Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival &amp; Thrown.<br /> <b>Serenity:</b> Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Medicine, Performance, Presence &amp; Socialize<br /> <b>Battles:</b> Archery, Athletics, Brawl, Melee, Presence, Resistance &amp; War<br /> <b>Secrets:</b> Integrity, Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth &amp; Thrown<br /> <b>Endings:</b> Awareness, Brawl, Bureaucracy, Integrity, Medicine, Occult &amp; Stealth</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your ability spreads make Journeys and Battles too similar to Night and Dawn caste's spread. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:25:56-08:00","id":806465,"title":"","content":"Journeys and Night don't have much in common. Athletics, Dodge, and Ride...there are plenty of three-ability matches in this setup. And in almost any setup, actually. Each Solar Caste has access to roughly a third of the list, so this sort of thing is hard to avoid.<br /> <br /> Battles and Dawn, yeah. But I'm fine with that. Fighting is pretty similar to Battles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=806008#post806008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of allowing martial arts to mix with Sidereal charms of an appropriate type is an interesting one. I think it would be ok off the top of my head, but I'd want to have a look at some combinations before I say definitively. Maybe make it a keyword that allows specific charms to cross over?<br /> <br /> Actually that pairs up somewhat with an idea I had to allow Sidereals to cross-apply certain charms from different combat abilities together. So because they are about changing circumstance rather than excellence they might be better able to use existing knowledge in a parallel way. Not sure whether it would homogenise things too much and detract from the uniqueness of the different styles of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>MA styles are all cross-applicable apart from weapon differences, and that seems to work. Think of each Sidereal combat Charmtree as a Martial Art and it all ought to work fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=806008#post806008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your ability spread for the castes. I'm not set on the idea of having 7 abilities to pick from for each caste I just thought I'd put it forward and see what people said. I agree that Sids should probably be more structured in terms of their castes than Solars though. I might make some changes to the abilities based on your suggestions, probably not all of them though, as I'm rather attached to the Secrets caste having Socialize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, good idea. That'd be a suitable replacement for Thrown.<br /> <br /> Anyway...are you interested in Charm suggestions or a point-by-point critique?<br /> <br /> I might have one or the other in me, but I don't want to do it if it's not appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T03:04:39-08:00","id":806870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=806465#post806465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway...are you interested in Charm suggestions or a point-by-point critique?<br /> <br /> I might have one or the other in me, but I don't want to do it if it's not appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either would be great honestly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Whichever you feel like doing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T20:33:41-08:00","id":807561,"title":"","content":"I was creating a Chosen of Endings and noticed that the colleges were wrong. Integrity is The Rising Smoke instead of the Mast. (Or at least it was in Second Edition. I don't know much about First Edition)<br /> <br /> For my sanity, I wrote out the colleges<br /> <br /> Archery - The Quiver <br /> Athletics - The Banner<br /> Awareness - The Crow <br /> Brawl - The Sword?<br /> Bureaucracy - The Haywain <br /> Craft - The Peacock <br /> Dodge - The Ewer <br /> Integrity - The Rising Smoke <br /> Investigation - The Key<br /> Larceny - The Guardians<br /> Linguistics - The Pillar<br /> Lore - The Treasure Trove<br /> Martial Arts - The Sword<br /> Medicine - The Corpse<br /> Melee - The Spear<br /> Occult - The Sorcerer<br /> Performance - The Musician<br /> Presence - The Gauntlet <br /> Resistance - The Mast <br /> Ride - The Messenger<br /> Sail - The Captain<br /> Socialize - The Lovers<br /> Stealth - The Mask<br /> Survival - The Ship's Wheel<br /> Thrown - The Gull <br /> War - The Shield<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T22:03:04-08:00","id":807607,"title":"","content":"For some reason, Sidereal War is what I had inspiration for.<br /> <br /> <b>Unfortunate Enemies Of Fate</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m (+1wp); <b>Mins:</b> War 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> This Charm supplements a Strategic Maneuver roll. The Sidereal may attempt to implement stratagems that have nothing to do with conventional planning and everything to do with luck. The Sidereal's favoured army becomes &quot;lucky&quot;, and their enemies become &quot;unlucky&quot;. Examples of stratagems that may be implemented with this Charm include:<br /> <br /> Unfortunate Accidents (threshold 1): Distribute twice the number of threshold successes among the enemy army as damage dice. The dice are lethal and decisive against individual characters, or dice of Magnitude damage against battle groups. Either way, they double 10s.<br /> <br /> Spiteful Sidereal Strategy (threshold 1): Horrible things happen to the enemy commander. They have no effect on the upcoming battle, and often occur after it, but they're nasty. Exactly how nasty depends on the number of threshold successes. 1 success might get the enemy robbed. 10 successes might cause their house to burn down in a fire that kills their husband and children, cause their husband's family to blame and hate them, give their beloved dog rabies, blight their farmland, infect them with syphilis, and drop a tree on their head.<br /> <br /> Plague (threshold 2): Each battle group or character in the enemy army must roll (Stamina + Resistance) against a difficulty of (threshold successes - 1, max 5). Each battle group that fails takes (threshold successes + 1) dice of lethal or Magnitude damage with double 10s. A battle group which takes 3 or more damage this way takes a -1 penalty to rolls and Defenses in the upcoming battle unless their leader fields only healthy soldiers and subtracts a point from the battle group's Size. Doing so also removes the damage from the plague. Characters which fail the resistance roll instead develop a disease with Morbidity of (threshold successes, max 5) at the Major Symptom level.<br /> <br /> Ammunition Shortage (threshold 3): Somehow, the enemy army runs short of arrows. Each enemy unit of archers may only attack twice before switching to melee weapons in the upcoming battle. They may conserve ammunition by taking a -2 penalty to their attack roll, which causes that attack roll to count as half an attack.<br /> <br /> For an additional 1wp, the Sidereal may use this Charm to make a Strategic Maneuver roll for an army that they're not leading. If they do so, and they get more successes than the leader of that army on that roll, then that leader's roll and chosen strategem are replaced by the Sidereal's. When using Unfortunate Enemies Of Fate this way, the Sidereal must select a strategy that the army could implement without actually planning to. Selecting a location for the battle is fine, causing unfortunate accidents for the other army is fine, causing the favoured army to create fortifications is not.<br /> <br /> <i>Sidereal War should make you really good at meddling in battles between mortals without anyone noticing. Not sure about the balance on the stratagems.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Fateful Lieutenant Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> War 4, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Unfortunate Enemies Of Fate<br /> <br /> When another character asks the Sidereal for advice and assistance in planning their battle strategy, the Sidereal may use their War Excellency to enhance that character's Strategic Maneuver rolls. If that character then implements their stratagem with successes to spare, they may use the extra successes to activate any stratagem available to a character using Unfortunate Enemies Of Fate.<br /> <br /> When advising a character with the Four Glories Meditation Charm, the Sidereal changes the limit on what they may reduce the TN to to 3.<br /> <br /> <i>Sidereals are supposed to be supremely good advisors, right? Particularly for Solars.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Selecting Survivors</b><br /> <b>\u200bCost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> War 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Predestined Triumph Method<br /> <br /> This Charm increases the TN of a damage roll against a battle group by 1. In addition, it allows the Sidereal to select (Essence) people in that battle group. Those people will suffer no serious harm from the attack. Even if the battle group is destroyed, they'll only flee or be knocked unconscious. This Charm cannot protect characters who are being deliberately targeted by the enemy.<br /> <br /> <i>I figure Sidereals need some way to keep soldiers with important destinies from being cut down. Also useful for protecting friends and family members.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T02:50:27-08:00","id":807745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=807561#post807561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was creating a Chosen of Endings and noticed that the colleges were wrong. Integrity is The Rising Smoke instead of the Mast. (Or at least it was in Second Edition. I don't know much about First Edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I admittedly took a couple of liberties with moving some of the college names around to other abilities. However I did so in order to get what I felt was a better fit to the pairings. For example The Gauntlet was originally Brawl in 1st Ed, but then got moved to Presence in 2nd due to Brawl no longer being a thing. Likewise The Rising Smoke was paired with Athletics in 1st Ed. To me it felt like The Rising smoke was a better match than The Banner for Athletics and therefore The Mast was more appropriate for Integrity.<br /> <br /> These are the abilities who had their pairings changed and a little of my thoughts on why. If you disagree on any of them please comment and I'll certainly look at them again.<br /> <br /> Athletics - The Banner &gt; <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><i>The Rising Smoke: Was originally this in 1st Ed. The Banner doesn't feel like a good fit, especially when compared to say War.</i></span><br /> Brawl - The Sword? &gt; <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><i>The Gauntlet: </i><i>Was this in 1st Ed. With there now effectively being 26 abilities (Martial Arts) it made sense for these two to be under the same college rather than coming up with a 26th college and all the hassle that comes with that decision.</i></span><br /> Integrity - The Rising Smoke &gt; <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><i>The Mast: Feels like a better fit for Integrity. The centre of things, steadfast and solid. I guess it would be quite easy to swap with The Shield (Resistance) though as it is also a symbol of physical strength.</i></span><br /> Martial Arts - The Sword &gt; <i><span style=\"color:#8B4513\">The Gauntlet: Mainly here because of the close ties between Brawl and Martial Arts. If I were looking to maintain the status quo more I would move this and Brawl back to The Sword and leave The Gauntlet with Presence.</span></i><br /> Presence - The Gauntlet &gt; <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><i>The Sword: Probably the pairing I am least happy with, but using your force of personality like a sword to cut through opposition feels like a reasonable enough connection to work.</i></span><br /> Resistance - The Mast &gt;<span style=\"color:#8B4513\"> <i>The Shield: Heroism, fearlessness and protection are the stated correlations for this college and they feel to me like pretty good fits for Resistance.</i></span><br /> War - The Shield &gt; <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><i>The Banner: Why oh why wasn't The Banner tied to War? Instead it moved from Presence (a good fit) to Athletics (a much worse fit). I put it here because it just makes too much sense to not do it.</i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=807607#post807607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some awesome looking charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Those look really nice. I'm not too certain on the balance of the strategems either, but they don't appear to be too much at a first look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T05:48:52-08:00","id":807801,"title":"","content":"I'll admit some of the pairings did look weird in Ex2. I think the Developers where trying to stick with certain themes around castes. For example, Journeys got a ship theme. Not really necessary with ability spreads in Ex3.<br /> <br /> I would make Melee - the Sword, Atheltics - the Spear, and Presence - the Rising Smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-13-2016, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T12:07:45-08:00","id":808123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=807801#post807801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit some of the pairings did look weird in Ex2. I think the Developers where trying to stick with certain themes around castes. For example, Journeys got a ship theme. Not really necessary with ability spreads in Ex3.<br /> <br /> I would make Melee - the Sword, Atheltics - the Spear, and Presence - the Rising Smoke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I disagree pretty strong with the MA/Gauntlet, Melee/Sword association. I think those miss the point of the association, which is not &quot;hey a gauntlet is like a fist right?&quot;<br /> <br /> The essential distinction drawn between the Sword and Spear constellations is that spears are a weapon that are particularly associated with soldiers and armies, with combat <i>in a battle</i>. The writeup talks about discipline because when massed spearmen go up against each other the most important thing to do is hold together. Swords are contrasted as a weapon solely for killing, in any context, and as a more individual weapon.<br /> <br /> Thus the Spear belongs in Battles and with Melee, and the Sword belongs in Endings and with Martial Arts (or Brawl - you also aren't likely to have a big company of troops fighting with Brawl).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T00:39:49-08:00","id":808501,"title":"","content":"Well the Gauntlet association was an extension of it being paired with 1st Ed Brawl, but looking at the actual Colleges I think you're right about the Gauntlet being more Battles and the Sword being more Ending in theme. I'm going to go through and swap those around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T19:50:36-08:00","id":813108,"title":"","content":"Fiddled with Craft a bit to make it fit the way I do Craft. <br /> <br /> Aiming to make Sidereals better at big Artifacts than small ones here. Also trying to play up the weirdness of Sidereal magic a bit; Sidereals have nothing that lets them cover the entirety of Craft, but they do have easy access to five specific fields.<br /> <br /> If it's not here, I didn't change it.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental Vision</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> <br /> There are five crafts which represent the elements to the Sidereal Exalted. They are<br /> <br /> <b>Air:</b> Painting<br /> <b>Earth:</b> Architecture<br /> <b>Fire:</b> Weapon-smithing<br /> <b>Wood:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Water:</b> Cooking<br /> <br /> Each costs only 1xp or 1/3 of a bonus point to a Sidereal with this Charm. A Sidereal who already has such specialties is refunded 2xp for each upon buying this Charm. In addition, any elemental or Terrestrial Exalt of an element that the Sidereal has the associated Craft for is treated as though they had a Minor Tie of respect for the Sidereal. Elementals and Terrestrials with Major or Defining Ties for the Sidereal ignore this effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Elegant Patterns of Fate</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 3, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> <br /> This Charm reduces the difficulty of an Artifact or Manse creation or repair roll by half.<br /> <br /> <b>Wonder-Birthing Midwife</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 5, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Mending Warped Designs<br /> <br /> This Charm converts all dice on an artifact or manse creation or repair roll to successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Implicit Construction Methodology</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m, 1wp, 1hl;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Predestined Delivery Shaping, Wonder-Birthing Midwife<br /> <br /> The Sidereal's prayer strip transforms into a band of blue light that wraps around the Sidereal's wrists as the Sidereal touches an object or materials that could be used to make one. For as long as the Sidereal keeps their motes committed, the object builds or repairs itself. Mundane objects are built or repaired at 10 times normal speed, while non-Legendary Artifacts shorten their interval to two weeks or half a session and Legendary Artifacts shorten their interval to a month or a session. Tools are not required, and if there's no workshop available Implicit Construction Methodology acts as though it had a basic workshop for the purpose of calculating the Terminus of an Artifact or Manse creation or repair roll.<br /> <br /> Implicit Construction Methodology does not roll to build or repair the object. It simply applies (Intelligence + Craft + stunt rating x 2 + Essence x 2) successes each time it would roll, and halves the difficulty of any Artifact or Manse construction or repair roll. The Sidereal's player may stunt the object's construction or repair even if their character isn't present, describing how the item comes together.<br /> <br /> This Charm cannot be used to build or repair anything the Sidereal could not normally use Craft to build or repair. Moonsilver reacts dangerously with this charm and must thus be worked normally.<br /> <br /> PS: Might also be a good idea to change World-Shaping Artistic Vision. -1 TN feels less useful now that it's so easily available to Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T00:44:10-08:00","id":813225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=813108#post813108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: Might also be a good idea to change World-Shaping Artistic Vision. -1 TN feels less useful now that it's so easily available to Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but a permanent -1TN that applies across abilities and colleges still feels worth a charm to me. I realise that it didn't actually say that it applied across all abilities before, but that was the intention, so I've fixed the text. If you made the speciality Swords then you'd get that bonus when ever you use a sword, craft a sword and in the college of the Sword (plus other thing I can't think of just now). If you were to chose a specific area of creation then you would be significantly better off whilst doing anything in that area, pretty much regardless of context. It also works well IMO with the Sidereal theme of working behind the scenes as using this they could easily get away with spending less essence to achieve their goals. Maybe I could add a way to rearrange the specialities, so that it becomes more like The Methodology of Secrets? Then it would allow Sidereals to ultra focus on their objective.<br /> <br /> <br /> PS: Oh and I like the craft charms. I've read your thread on Craft and like the look of it, but I'm not in a game as a crafter at the moment so I have no opportunity to test them or compare outside of theory-crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T01:09:34-08:00","id":813235,"title":"","content":"In retrospect, &quot;less useful&quot; isn't right. Saving motes is pretty powerful.<br /> <br /> But it's not exciting. Within a multi-ability specialty, you get a 1m discount on your excellency. Yay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T01:19:08-08:00","id":813238,"title":"","content":"Ok. I'll definitely give you that one :P It's certainly not exciting, but then anything that 'merely' adds dice/reduce target numbers isn't either and yet we still need some of those. And it's pretty much the only charm in Craft that does 'dice adding' of any kind outside of the excellency, so I think I'm fine with it being a little boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T13:19:39-08:00","id":813597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=784007#post784007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <hr /> <u><b>Craft</b></u><br /> <b>Elemental Vision</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> There are 5 versions of this charm, one for each of the elements. Different crafts resonate with different elements, so each element requires a different craft ability to buy the apprpriate charm:<br /> <b>Air:</b> calligraphy, jewelery making, glassblowing<br /> <b>Earth:</b> masonry, stone cutting, creating earthworks<br /> <b>Fire:</b> blacksmithing, creating ceramics<br /> <b>Wood:</b> carpentry, weaving, flower arranging<br /> <b>Water:</b> cooking, brewing, leather working<br /> The charm gives a Minor Tie of Respect for the Sidereal in any elementals, dragon-bloods or god of the corresponding element.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all splats need a version of Supreme Celestial Focus, as an Exalt Fix for the Crafting XP sink. So I would have this charm also let you spend gxp to raise the associated craft from 1-5, with a limit of (Essence) crafts.<br /> <br /> Possible additional changes are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It can be retroactive - if you buy it for a craft you already have rated above 1, you can also use gxp to refund the ranks you've already purchased. (This is a minor change but seems fairest.)</li> <li>Rather than having to purchasing it five times (which is pretty expensive!), you purchase it once, and it applies to at most (Essence) different elements.</li> </ol><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=813108#post813108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Elemental Vision</b><br /> <b>Cost: -</b>;<b> Mins:</b> Craft 2, Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> <br /> There are five crafts which represent the elements to the Sidereal Exalted. They are<br /> <br /> <b>Air:</b> Painting<br /> <b>Earth:</b> Architecture<br /> <b>Fire:</b> Weapon-smithing<br /> <b>Wood:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Water:</b> Cooking<br /> <br /> Each costs only 1xp or 1/3 of a bonus point to a Sidereal with this Charm. A Sidereal who already has such specialties is refunded 2xp for each upon buying this Charm. In addition, any elemental or Terrestrial Exalt of an element that the Sidereal has the associated Craft for is treated as though they had a Minor Tie of respect for the Sidereal. Elementals and Terrestrials with Major or Defining Ties for the Sidereal ignore this effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Calligraphy is better for Air (prayer strips). Weaving is obviously correct. But Architecture and Cooking just seem... insufficiently esoteric in that singularly Sidereal fashion. Not sure what they should be instead. Maybe sculpture for Earth and Brewing for Water?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:14:52-08:00","id":813644,"title":"","content":"Calligraphy is too Linguistics-y for my taste.<br /> <br /> Considered brewing, but I wanted to go with something that would actually get used. And Craft is under Serenity, so I think there's a place for simple home-y stuff in it.<br /> <br /> Architecture might as well go. I picked it because it was obviously earth-y and useful for stuff like manses. Thing is, I'm not sure if sculpture is really any better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:20:29-08:00","id":813646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=813644#post813644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calligraphy is too Linguistics-y for my taste.<br /> <br /> Considered brewing, but I wanted to go with something that would actually get used. And Craft is under Serenity, so I think there's a place for simple home-y stuff in it.<br /> <br /> Architecture might as well go. I picked it because it was obviously earth-y and useful for stuff like manses. Thing is, I'm not sure if sculpture is really any better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the editions have been pretty consistent in the idea that linguistics is about the words, <i>not</i> the actual artistic quality of the handwriting. Calligraphy was an explicit example of an Air craft in the 2e core book.<br /> <br /> Also, as I said, prayer strips!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:34:57-08:00","id":813659,"title":"","content":"There are totally calligraphy Charms in Linguistics, though. Flawless Brush Discipline, Flowing Elegant Hand, Moving The Unseen Hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:41:31-08:00","id":813754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=813659#post813659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are totally calligraphy Charms in Linguistics, though. Flawless Brush Discipline, Flowing Elegant Hand, Moving The Unseen Hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh, you're right, there's even a sidebar claiming that calligraphy is governed by Linguistics now. Mea culpa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T17:38:52-08:00","id":813772,"title":"","content":"...I actually feel kinda silly for not seeing that sidebar when I went looking for calligraphy Charms.<br /> <br /> Reading it now, it seems to shoot holes in my desire for Craft mapmaking Charms. But whatever, if I'm rewriting an Ability I can change that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T23:57:52-08:00","id":813952,"title":"","content":"I'd love a sidereal war charm called for the want of a nail and with a thematically linked effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T12:40:40-08:00","id":814973,"title":"","content":"Maybe using it gives you some kind of minor task. If you perform that task, your target gets TN 10 on a single roll later. You don't choose which roll, but you can specify more or less what you want them to fail at. It will generally be an important roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T04:42:32-08:00","id":820881,"title":"","content":"Just a brief update. I've been pretty slow in getting this stage of the project updated so not much has happened over the last week or so. Resplendent Effects are still in progress and I've started writing up notes on how I want the second half of the Sidereal charms to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=813952#post813952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love a sidereal war charm called for the want of a nail and with a thematically linked effect</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say that I came at this from what appears to be the opposite direction to Sanctaphrax. I thought that a charm that permanently allows you to reduce dice penalties by one that relate to not having the right equipment for the job. It would be like you can always find something appropriate to what you want to do. (Trying to pick a lock with no tools, well these two splinters should work good enough.) I was also considering making it so that it could cancel the initiative use of improvised weapons too, though that might be a bit much for one charm to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T05:21:25-07:00","id":893214,"title":"","content":"Ok. So I've been very remiss in keeping up with this project. Honestly, the Resplendency powers just crushed me. I got through the one I could, but then just hit a brick wall in terms of creativity and enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> Been drifting back through things in the last couple of weeks though and have started adding some expansions to the earlier charm trees, which I've had written up for a while. The expansions will vary in size quite a lot as I end up with more ideas for some things than others.<br /> <br /> I'm carefully avoiding Resplendencies for now until I can come up with enough willpower to dive into them again or an alternative, simpler, approach. A thought I had was that I could turn the effects I have now into 'proper' charms and instead give resplendent destinies a small 'generic' power. I know its not a hugely exciting proposition, but I think something along the lines of: &quot;While in a resplendent destiny the Sidereal's dice cap for the related ability is increased by one.&quot; might work.<br /> <br /> Anyway I'm hoping to keep going with this. If only to provide an alternative to wasteven's works. (I really like what he's doing, but his plan is different enough that I think its worth me continuing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T05:34:00-07:00","id":893217,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear it. I hope it turns out easier 